\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late Vs US Dlr After ECB Issing Remarks  \b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2005\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar strengthened late Wednesday in Asia after a senior European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Asian countries needed to do more to accommodate the weakening U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were flat to weaker, in line with weakness in U.S. Treasurys late Tuesday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6390, down from S$1.6421 late in Asia Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6376 and S$1.6420 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 ECB chief economist Otmar Issing said at a conference Tuesday that Asian nations, and China in particular, aren't contributing enough to reduce global imbalances stemming from the large U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "China is still putting off its contribution, but it will no doubt at some stage act," he said, reiterating comments by other European policy-makers that Europe has unfairly borne the brunt of weakness in the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said Issing's remarks reaffirmed the view that U.S. and eurozone policy-makers are still keen on pressuring China to move to a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate regime from its current system that effectively pegs the yuan to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Chinese authorities are widely expected to announce a change to the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate regime this year. Any such change could put upward pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Singapore dollar, against the U.S. dollar and the euro.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a one-week low of S$1.6363 in New York late Tuesday before rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar's slide, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that the MAS might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in Wednesday's Asian session sparked short-covering among interbank players, boosting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as S$1.6420 in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 But other players capitalized on the U.S. dollar's rally, selling the U.S. unit back down to just below the psychologically important S$1.6400 level in the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 "For now, we can expect the dollar-sing to trade around S$1.6350-S$1.6450. Only a decisive move above S$1.6420 would take out the downside bias," said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate         1.8750%  1.8125% \par Two-year bond yield    1.77%    1.75% \par 10-year bond yield     2.83%    2.81% \par Two-year swap offer    1.99%    1.96% \par 10-year swap offer     3.05%    3.05% \par 2-10-year swap spread  106 BPs  109 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\uc2 \f2  \par  \par    -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 12-01-05 0704GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI000