\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won leads drop on US rate worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2005\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led\par declines in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, following an\par overnight drop of nearly 2 percent in the yen against the\par dollar, on worries the U.S. Federal Reserve might raise rates\par faster than expected.\par     The won plunged 1 percent to 1,049 per dollar. The won's 15\par percent gain in 2004, which made it Asia's best performing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , had led the government to increase dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect local exporters as local spending\par slowed.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar Taiwan dollar Thai baht and the\par Indonesian rupiah all lost about half a percent.\par     Higher trading volumes after the year-end holidays fuelled\par the dollar's recovery from multi-year lows.\par     The dollar's advance was helped by the release of minutes\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  from the U.S. Federal Reserve's Dec. 14 meeting, which said   \par \par \uc2  current benchmark interest rates were too low to check   \par \par \uc2  inflation.   \par \par \uc2  "The general sentiment is pointing to a 100 basis points   \par \par \uc2  increase in Fed rates for the whole year," said Christy Tan, a   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at 4CAST Ltd. in Singapore. "Whether they're   \par \par \uc2  going to be more aggressive is yet to be seen."   \par \par \uc2  Higher U.S. interest rates make U.S. bonds and other assets   \par \par \uc2  more attractive to Asian investors. So, a sharper-than-expected   \par \par \uc2  increase in U.S. interest rates could lead to money flowing out   \par \par \uc2  of Asian bonds and stocks, dragging regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.   \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen Asia's most actively traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,   \par \par \uc2  plunged to 104.80 per dollar in overnight trading and steadied   \par \par \uc2  at that level on Wednesday, compared with 102.53 in late Asian   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "It's going to be pretty much a yen-play for the next few\par days," said Tan.\par     LONGER-TERM TREND\par     Tan didn't expect the dollar's declining trend to change in\par the longer term as investors remain worried about the record\par U.S. current account deficit.\par     The won surged 15 percent last year on those worries. Most\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts expect the won, the Taiwan dollar, the baht and the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indian rupee to extend their gains this year on concern that\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. would be unable to attract enough overseas capital\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "I don't think fundamentally that view has changed," said\par Tan.\par     The Singapore dollar one of Asia's most actively traded\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , weakened to a three-week low of 1.6510 per dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in overnight trades, compared with 1.6369 in late Asian trading\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also fell as expectations eased that China\par might revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan.\par     China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which started on Tuesday a three-day\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting with local bankers, repeated its policy of keeping the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yuan "basically stable" even as it pledged to push ahead with\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Speculation that China may let the tightly-controlled yuan\par appreciate this year had bolstered Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last year.\par     "It turned out to be quite a disappointment," said Tan,\par referring to the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statement after the first\par day of the meeting.\par     "There was nothing new," she said. "As long as speculative\par pressures on a revaluation stays high, chances of any change\par will be reduced."\par     The premium on the three-month yuan non-deliverable\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards, agreements that speculators use to bet on any change\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the yuan's value in the future, plunged to 1.5 percent on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday from a one-year high of about 2.2 percent traded last\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The premium on the six-month yuan NDF dropped to 3.1\par percent from a record high of 4 percent reached last week.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0223 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.42         102.53       -1.81\par  Sing dlr        1.6460         1.6369       -0.55\par  Taiwan dlr      32.010         31.846       -0.51\par  Korean won     1047.40        1038.50       -0.85\par  Baht             39.13          38.92       -0.54\par  Peso             56.22          56.15       -0.12\par  Rupiah         9305.00        9272.00       -0.35\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \h