\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah gains on debt-relief hopes.  \b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2005\par 09:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah, Asia's\par worst-performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2004, gained on Tuesday on hope\par overseas lenders may cut the country's foreign debt to help it\par recover from the tsunami disaster.\par  \par     The rupiah        gained as much as half a percent, to\par 9,255 per dollar, compared with late Asian trades on Monday.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were little changed, as concerns\par about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weighed on a\par largely bullish outlook for the regional units this year.\par     Indonesia might gain the most if, as expected, the Paris\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Club of creditor governments offered debt relief to countries  \f28 \par \par \uc2 hit by the Dec. 26 disaster, analysts said. The forum is to  \par \par \uc2 meet on Jan. 12.  \par \par \uc2 "The Italians have suggested cutting Indonesia's foreign  \par \par \uc2 debt," said Song Seng Wun, an economist at Singapore-based G.K.  \par \par \uc2 Goh Securities. "It's a nice gesture. Every little bit will  \par \par \uc2 help."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     G.K. Goh expects the rupiah to strengthen to 8,500 per\par dollar by the end of this year.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RISK\par     The South Korean won       , the Taiwan dollar          and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Singapore dollar were held back by worries central  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks might step up dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap gains in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bolster exports that are seen slowing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won rose to a seven-year high and the Taiwan dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ended local trading on Monday at 31.845 per dollar, a four-year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 closing high. The Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed Tuesday at 31.846 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the Taiwan dollar and the won may outperform  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian rivals in 2005 as the U.S. current account deficit  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 extends the dollar's decline against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fourth straight year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, risks of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 threatening their outlook for the next few weeks, dealers  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 reserves rose 3.4 percent in December, indicating authorities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had stepped up attempts to slow the surge in the won, which  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gained 15 percent in 2004 to be Asia's best performing  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A finance ministry official said the government would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increase, if necessary, the ceiling on bond sales to fund  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The finance ministry appears poised to step up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Claudio Piron, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at JP Morgan Chase in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has so  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 far slowed the won's gain rather than reversed it, he said,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 adding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not at any unprecedented  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 level.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht  and the Indian rupee        gained\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 modestly  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts downplayed the impact of the tsunami.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The shock to regional tourism is unlikely to reach  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SARS-like proportions," said Piron. "Indonesia was not hit in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 major tourist spots, India has small reliance on tourist  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 receipts and Malaysia was relatively less hit."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan Chase cut its first-quarter growth outlook for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand but said it would be wrong to view the calamity as an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic trend-turning event, despite its human costs.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0805 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 