rt, said it expects Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bear the brunt of a weak U.S. dollar, projecting that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fall to S$1.6100-S$1.6300 at the end of the first quarter of next year.  \par \par \uc2 Following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest   Previous \par Two-year bond yield  1.63%    1.62% \par 10-year bond yield   2.73%    2.73% \par Two-year swap offer  1.80%    1.80% \par 10-year swap offer   2.95%    2.95% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  115 BPs  115 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\uc2 \f2  \par  \par    -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Paul Baylis \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 29-12-04 0716GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041229e0ct00058\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
