\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Gains capped by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2004\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Korean won, Taiwan dollar\par and Singapore dollar set 2-week highs in holiday-thinned\par trading, but fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped further\par gains on Friday as the U.S. dollar hit fresh lows against the\par euro and ceded ground to the Japanese yen.\par     The won                   was up about a quarter percent,\par coming off a high near 1,045 per dollar amid worries the Bank\par of Korea would buy dollars. Its gains outpaced even the yen's\par since Thursday and have put it on track to become Asia's top\par performer in 2004.\par     It has risen about 14 percent so far this year. The Taiwan\par dollar, the next best performer, has managed less than half\par that gain.\par     A mixed batch of U.S. data, including weak new home sales,\par and technical factors drove the euro up to above $1.35. The yen\par moved more cautiously, and was quoted around 103.72/75 at 0800\par GMT.\par     Trading volumes have shrunk in the final weeks of the year.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the euro had a good chance of appreciating because\par markets had unwound their heavy euro long positions in the\par first half of December, as data from the U.S. Commodity Futures\par Commission showed.\par     "We expect the U.S. dollar to weaken further in the first\par half of 2005 against developed and emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par given the U.S. twin deficits and the perception the U.S.\par authorities are happy to see the U.S. dollar weaken, so long as\par the process is orderly," Standard Chartered Bank said in a\par commentary.\par     The Singapore dollar        moved between 1.6360 and 1.64,\par with the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surfacing intermittently as local banks bought U.S.\par dollars.\par     Even offshore premiums on the Chinese yuan were higher as\par markets disregarded a statement from authorities earlier this\par week that they had no plans to shift their stance on the\par tightly managed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Speculation has intensified in the market that China might\par shift its stance before the end of the year. But a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par spokesman said on Wednesday, "At present there is no change in\par the exchange rate policy."\par     One-year non-deliverable forwards           were quoted at\par 4,900 points, pricing in a 6.3 percent appreciation in the yuan\par in a year. The yuan is effectively pegged around 8.28 per U.S.\par dollar.\par     "There is no extra special news that has triggered the\par speculation. I think it is the broad dollar trend," said Tai\par Hui, Standard Chartered Bank's economist for Greater China,\par referring to the move in NDFs.\par  \par     Standard Chartered expects China to widen the yuan's narrow\par trading band in the first half of 2005.\par     Meanwhile, the Taiwan dollar retreated from 32.05 as\par markets trod warily, fearing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  near the 32 mark.\par     Hui said 32 was a level to watch. Yet recent economic data\par had been strong and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might not be averse to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, he said.\par     Taiwan's export orders showed a robust 30 percent annual\par growth in November.\par     "Export orders data released yesterday was still quite\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strong," said Hui. "From that perspective, I don't think the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is concerned about the level. Smoothing out the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ups and downs in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be their objective."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets in the Philippines were closed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah traded conclusively on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 firmer side of 9,300 for the first time in a week, seemingly  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overcoming recent downward pressures from commercial outflows,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 political and security worries.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0820 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.74         103.95       +0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.6392         1.6411       +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      32.190         32.228       +0.12\par  Korean won     1047.80        1050.40       +0.25\par  Baht             38.99          39.03       +0.10\par  Peso             56.00          56.13       +0.23\par  Rupiah         9265.00        9290.00       +0.27\par  Rupee            43.83          43.76       -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.74         107.31       +3.44\par  Sing dlr        1.6392         1.6978       +3.57\par  Taiwan dlr      32.190         33.978       +5.55\