\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dollar dips, others higher.  \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2004\par 09:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 23 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on\par Thursday in holiday-thinned trading as the U.S. dollar softened\par against the euro and Japanese yen.\par     The regionals gained despite weakness in local stocks and\par even after China had quashed rumours of an imminent change in\par yuan policy on Wednesday. Malaysia also said it would keep its\par peg for now, robbing markets of a big reason to buy the Asians.\par     The Korean won                   hit a two-week peak of\par 1,050.5 a dollar. The Taiwan dollar  also firmed to a\par two-week high before trimming its gains.\par     The Singapore dollar        moved to one-week high near\par 1.6370, before fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dragged the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down to 1.6420.\par  \par     "It is the underlying concerns about the U.S. dollar," said\par DBS Bank strategist Chua Hak Bin.\par     The euro        rallied to $1.3450 per dollar, its highest\par since Dec.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  7 when it hit a record high of $1.3470, after\par stop-loss orders were triggered.\par     The yen        straddled 104 per dollar, although volumes\par were low with Japanese markets closed for the Emperor's\par birthday.\par     Jimmy Koh, head of research at United Overseas Bank, said\par most of the speculative money was still finding its way into\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Despite Chinese officials dismissing as rumours talk of a\par change in yuan policy during the year-end holidays, offshore\par non-deliverable forwards showed the yuan at a high premium.\par     One-year NDFs were quoted at 4,600 points, pricing in a 5.9\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent appreciation in the yuan and not far from Wednesday's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 peak of 4,800 points. The yuan is pegged around 8.28 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "By and large markets are positioning for a yuan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revaluation in 2005," Koh said, adding that would underpin  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Regional stock markets had opened higher after  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a rally in U.S. stocks led by data showing sturdy U.S. economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth and a fall in oil prices. But most indices reversed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 later.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reined in the Thai baht\par  , which struggled to rise past 39 per dollar.\par     Korea's finance ministry repeated its view that the won's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent advance was too rapid. The won has jumped nearly 10  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent since early October, making it Asia's best performer  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar so far this year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah rose over a quarter percent,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 testing ground on the firmer side of 9,300.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0805 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par 