\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Higher on stocks, yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2004\par 03:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 23 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on\par Thursday, aided by higher local stock markets and the yen,\par although traders said volumes were thin and moves exaggerated\par by a Japanese holiday and the approaching year-end.\par     Local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  advances surprised some traders, after China\par on Wednesday quashed rumours of a change in yuan policy by\par year-end and Malaysia said it would stay with a pegged exchange\par rate for now. That robbed local markets of a big reason to\par continue buying the Asians.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar was at a week's high near 1.6370, and\par the Korean won and Taiwan dollar were at 2-week peaks.\par     "I was cynical about the China revaluation theory in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 first place. There was never any clear indication China will  \f28 \par \par \uc2 move the renminbi," said Wong Keng Siong, strategist with Bank  \par \par \uc2 of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. "And I would not make much of these moves,  \par \par \uc2 activity is so thin."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Japanese markets were closed for the Emperor's birthday and\par the yen crawled to the firmer side of 104 per dollar.\par     Regional stock markets opened higher after a rally in U.S.\par stocks spurred by data showing sturdy U.S. economic growth and\par a fall in oil prices.\par     Fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reined in some regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , such as the won and Thai baht\par     The baht struggled to rise past 39 per dollar.\par     "That 39 level is quite sticky. Although the Bank of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand says it is hands-off the baht, it is quite obvious  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they are \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the forward and swap markets," Wong  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But analysts said authorities in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have less  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reason to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as speculation abated of a surprise yuan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revaluation by year-end, which eased upward pressure on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sing dollar. The Sing is considered a favoured proxy bet on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revaluation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Korea's finance ministry repeated that the won's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent advance was too rapid. The won has jumped nearly 10  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent since early October, making it Asia's best performer so  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 far this year.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0151 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.95         104.34       +0.38\par  Sing dlr        1.6381         1.6404       +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      32.205         32.300       +0.29\par  Korean won     1051.00        1053.50       +0.24\par  Baht             39.04          39.04       +0.00\par  Peso             56.04          56.12       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9305.00        9320.00       +0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.95         107.31       +3.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6381         1.6978       +3.64\par  Taiwan dlr      32.205         33.978       +5.51\par  Korean won     1051.00        1192.00      +13.42\par  Baht             39.04          39.59       +1.40\par  Peso             56.04          55.49       -0.99\par  Rupiah         9305.00        8410.00       -9.62\par  Rupee            43.83          45.60       +4.03.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041223e0cn0025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
