\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Edges Up Late; Government Bonds Weaker  \b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2004\par 08:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar edged higher against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Wednesday in thin trading, while Singapore government bonds were weaker across the board on profit-taking, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0730 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6410, down slightly from S$1.6420 late in Asia Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6400 and S$1.6425.  \par \par \uc2 With the approach of the Christmas holiday in the U.S. and many other countries at the end of this week, trading was confined to a narrow range and was largely driven by movements in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen throughout Wednesday's Asian session.  \par \par \uc2 Most market participants have already closed their books on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions for the year, with just a few of them tinkering with U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar positions.  \par \par \uc2 "Not much is happening. It's very quiet," said a Singapore dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have found strong support around the S$1.6390 level, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the past two sessions to stem the U.S. unit's slide against the local dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, however, the U.S. dollar faces somewhat strong resistance at S$1.6435, the downtrend line from the Dec. 10 high of S$1.6605, based on technical analysis.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair has formed a symmetrical triangle bounded by the downtrend line from the Dec. 10 peak and by a minor uptrend line (now at S$1.6391) from the Dec. 15 low. The downtrend in 10-day momentum suggests the most likely direction of any breakout would be down, which would target the S$1.6200 area.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore government bond market, meanwhile, bucked the overnight trend of strength in the U.S. Treasurys market, as local bond yields rose along the curve, especially at the long end, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The brief break of the 2-year vs 10-year yield spread below the psychologically important 100 basis-point level early in the session prompted some players to unwind curve flatteners for profits.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest  Previous \par Two-year bond yield  1.56%   1.54% \par 10-year bond yield   2.60%   2.54% \par Two-year swap offer  1.77%   1.72% \par 10-year swap offer   2.85%   2.80% \par 2-10-yr swap spread: 108 BPs 108 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale [ 22-12-04 0753GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041222e0cm00099\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
