\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late In Thin Pre-Holiday Trading  \b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2004\par 07:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar edged up against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Monday in thin, range-bound trading ahead of holidays later this week.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices were flat to higher in subdued trading, dealers say.  \par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6457, down from S$1.6478 late in Asia Friday. It traded between S$1.6442 and S$1.6463 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Throughout the Asian session, the U.S. dollar hugged a very narrow range against the Singaporean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as many banks and other financial institutions that make the local market move have closed their books for this year.  \par \par \uc2 "It's hard to quote prices to clients," said a Singapore dealer, who pointed to a sharp reduction in market liquidity that typically occurs at year-end bookclosing.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volume in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is expected be low and largely directionless, with a public holiday in Japan on Thursday and in the U.S. on Friday, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi's economist Wong Keng Siong said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 "In an absence of fresh positive news, the Singapore dollar is likely to be range bound at S$1.6400-S$1.6600 per U.S. dollar this week," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Wong added that a "line of defense" may have been established at the S$1.6400 level and at the S$1.6300 level against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, either to stem the U.S. dollar's slide against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or to curb excessive volatility of the Singapore dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the U.S. unit fell to as low as S$1.6370, its lowest level since Dec. 8.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest  Previous \par Two-year bond yield  1.50%   1.53% \par 10-year bond yield   2.57%   2.57% \par Two-year swap offer  1.72%   1.69% \par 10-year swap offer   2.86%   2.85% \par 2-10-yr swap spread: 114 BPs 116 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 20-12-04 0648GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041220e0ck0005z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
