\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Sing dlr fall on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2004\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the\par Singapore dollar led Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down on Friday on worries\par central banks may step up dollar-buying to stem a two-month\par rally in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that may threaten exports.\par     The two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened almost a third of a percent\par each, taking the won to 1,060 per dollar and the Singapore\par dollar to 1.6482/1.6492 per dollar.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore checked\par rates with some banks -- a signal that it might be thinking of\par buying dollars.\par     The central banks of South Korea, Singapore and India have\par stepped up dollar buying since November to stem a rally sparked\par by concerns the United States seemed unable to attract enough\par capital from abroad to plug its record current account deficit.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea said Friday it had carried out further\par "smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the\par first half of December, boosting the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves by $3.4 billion in the fortnight to Dec. 15.\par  \par     "These levels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are not sustainable," said\par Sani Hamid, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST in Singapore.\par     Bank of Korea had to step up dollar-buying since November\par to absorb the dollars sold by local firms as exports soared, he\par said. But he added this may ease off.\par     "With technology exports slowing down next year, the\par current account surplus is likely to taper off a bit," he said.\par     The won has gained 13 percent this year, making it Asia's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surged to a seven-year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high this month against the dollar as exporters dumped their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar earnings on worries about the weakening dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE EXPORTS SLUMP  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar, which has underperformed the won, the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan dollar and the yen this year, weakened after the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government reported a higher-than-expected 9.1 percent decline  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the country's non-oil exports in November. A Reuters poll of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economists had forecast a 1.9 percent decline.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar is now on the weaker side of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted range within which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore maintains the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ABN AMRO Bank said in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 report, adding that gains are likely to be modest without a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 boost from overseas portfolio investments, like those seen in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea and Taiwan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah weakened as much as half a percent to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9,325 per dollar, closer to a 3-= month low reached on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday, on concerns about end-of-year purchase of dollars by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local companies to repay overseas debt.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hurt by a widening budget deficit and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increased security concerns as several countries warned their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 citizens not to travel to Indonesia during the holiday season.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah was unlikely to weaken further, Hamid said,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 because the government had received a $400 million loan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 committment from the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to help plug a widening budget shortfall.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ADB will disburse $100 million this week, a senior\par Indonesian finance ministry official said on Thursday.\par     The Indian rupee lost almost half a percent to 44.03 per\par dollar as stocks paused, after a run up this year.\par     Record foreign investments in Indian stocks this year and\par slowing inflation were likely to limit further losses, JP\par Morgan Chase and ABN AMRO said in separate reports.\par     The Indian government reported a decline in the rate of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increase in wholesale prices to 7.02 percent in the 12 months  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to Dec. 4, from 7.3 percent in the year through the previous  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0800 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.44         104.29       -0.14\par  Sing dlr        1.6477         1.6422       -0.33\par  Taiwan dlr      32.359         32.340       -0.06\par  Korean won     1059.90        1056.30       -0.34\par  Baht             39.30          39.16       -0.36\par  Peso             56.17          56.26       +0.15\par  Rupiah         9293.00        9270.00       -0.25\par  Rupee            44.04          43.85       -0.44\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.44         107.31       +2.75\par  Sing dlr        1.6477         1.6978       +3.04\par  Taiwan dlr      32.359         33.978       +5.00\par  Korean won     1059.90        1192.00      +12.46\par  Baht             39.30          39.59       +0.73\par  Peso             56.17          55.49       -1.22\par  Rupiah         9293.00        8410.00       -9.50\par  Rupee            44.04          45.60       +3.53.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041217e0ch007n4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
