\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Sing dlr fall on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2004\par 09:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the\par Singapore dollar led Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down on Friday on worries\par central banks may step up dollar-buying to stem a two-month\par rally in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that may threaten exports.\par     The two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened almost a third of a percent\par each, taking the won             to 1,060 per dollar and\par the Singapore dollar  to 1.6482/1.6492 per dollar.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore checked\par rates with some banks -- a signal that it might be thinking of\par buying dollars.\par     The central banks of South Korea, Singapore and India have\par stepped up dollar buying since November to stem a rally sparked\par by concerns the United States seemed unable to attract enough\par capital from abroad to plug its record current account deficit.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea said Friday it had carried out further\par "smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the\par first half of December, boosting the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves by $3.4 billion in the fortnight to Dec. 15.\par  \par     "These levels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are not sustainable," said\par Sani Hamid, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST in Singapore.\par     Bank of Korea had to step up dollar-buying since November\par to absorb the dollars sold by local firms as exports soared, he\par said. But he added this may ease off.\par     "With technology exports slowing down next year, the\par current account surplus is likely to taper off a bit," he said.\par     The won has gained 13 percent this year, making it Asia's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surged to a seven-year\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high this month against the dollar as exporters dumped their\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar earnings on worries about the weakening dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE EXPORTS SLUMP\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar  and the yen        this year, weakened\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the government reported a higher-than-expected 9.1\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent decline the country's non-oil exports in November. A\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters poll of economists had forecast a 1.9 percent decline.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar is now on the weaker side of the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted range within which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore maintains the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ABN AMRO Bank said in a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par report, adding that gains are likely to be modest without a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boost from overseas portfolio investments, like those seen in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea and Taiwan.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  weakened as much as half a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent to 9,325 per dollar, closer to a 3-= month low\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reached on Wednesday, on concerns about end-of-year purchase of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars by local companies to repay overseas debt.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hurt by a widening budget deficit and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par increased security concerns as several countries warned their\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par citizens not to travel to Indonesia during the holiday season.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was unlikely to weaken further, Hamid said,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because the government had received a $400 million loan\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par committment from the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ADB will disburse $100 million this week, a senior\par Indonesian finance ministry official said on Thursday.\par     The Indian rupee          lost almost half a percent to\par 44.03 per dollar as stocks paused, after a run up this year.\par     Record foreign investments in Indian stocks this year and\par slowing inflation were likely to limit further losses, JP\par Morgan Chase and ABN AMRO said in separate reports.\par     The Indian government reported a decline in the rate of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par increase in wholesale prices to 7.02 percent in the 12 months\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to Dec. 4, from 7.3 percent in the year through the previous\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0800 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen