\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Dollar up on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  hints, Asian shares dip.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Callus  \par \uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 7 (Reuters) - The dollar rallied on Tuesday on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hints, underpinning shares in Asian exporters, but stocks in the region were mostly lower on nerves over Japan economic data and Hong Kong IPOs due this week.   \par \par \uc2  Shares in Amcor (AMC.AX), the world's largest maker of plastic bottles, fell 8 percent on news it had ousted its chief executive after finding some staff may have acted illegally to drive up box prices.   \par \par \uc2  Crude oil continued a rally from three-month lows to stand above $43 a barrel, as traders eyed signals from OPEC that it might take action to stem a slide that knocked 14 percent off prices last week. The producer cartel meets in Cairo on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  Gold weakened as the dollar climbed, and Japanese government bonds were flat ahead of economic data out Wednesday and Thursday.   \par \par \uc2  On Monday, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro-zone finance ministers built on recent rhetoric against their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge, saying in a joint statement that sharp moves in exchange rates were unwelcome and that they were closely monitoring swings.   \par \par \uc2  "It hints at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they (the ECB and European finance ministries) together control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy for Europe," said Jake Moore, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank.   \par \par \uc2  "The market's getting a bit nervous and that's prompted a bit of profit-taking," he said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably not occur unless the euro rose to around $1.38.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was around $1.3408 against the euro , up slightly from late levels in New York, where it rose about 0.4 percent. It marked a record low of $1.3461 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought around 103.02 yen , little changed from late New York, where it rose 1 yen, due in part to concerns about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was well off a five-year low of 101.83 yen hit last week.   \par \par \uc2  GDP, IPOS AWAITED   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei stock average  fell 0.25 percent to 10,954.01\par by its mid-session close, Hong Kong's Hang Seng        was up 0.14\par percent at 14,283.58 in early trade, while an MSCI index of Asian\par non-Japan shares            was 0.46 percent lower at 255.79.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mitsui Trust Holdings Inc (8309.T), Japan's seventh-largest bank by\par assets, supported the Nikkei, climbing 4.1 percent after Goldman Sachs\par raised its rating on the stock to "outperform" from "in line". The\par broker said continued operating profit growth would give it enough\par retained earnings to pay back the funds it owes from a state bail-out\par in the late 1990s. Daiei Inc. (8263.T) jumped 7 percent, extending\par gains into a fifth straight session as foreign and domestic investors,\par including Wal-Mart Stores Inc. (WMT.N), queued up to submit proposals\par to the state-backed Industrial Revitalisation Corp. of Japan (IRCJ) for\par reviving the debt-laden retailer.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo traders said investors were on the sidelines ahead of revised\par gross domestic product (GDP) figures for the July-September quarter,\par due on Wednesday, and October machinery orders data due on Thursday to\par get a better idea of how Japan's economy is faring.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Nikkei is basically stuck around 11,000 and we're all waiting for\par a signal for which way to go next," said Koji Muneoka, head of domestic\par sales trading at HSBC in Tokyo.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Hong Kong all eyes were on two large IPOs - Air China and the Hong\par Kong Housing Authority's Link's property trust - due to raise a\par combined US$4.1 billion this week. Singapore's Straits Times  rose half\par a percent, led by Sembcorp (SWMS.SI), which announced a special\par dividend. Taiwan's benchmark index         dropped a third of a percent\par ahead of legislative elections on Saturday. Australia's S&P ASX 200\par     fell 0.31, dragged down by Amcor. South Korea's KOSPI         fell\par 0.61 percent. Global stocks as measured by the MSCI World Index\par   were down 0.36 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gold  fell to $452.75 an ounce from $454 overnight. January NYMEX crude\par        climbed 8 cents to $43.06. Ten-year JGB futures           were\par flat, yielding 1.4 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c70028o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
