\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fear forces retreat.  \b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 03:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 7 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par forced off their recent multi-year peaks on Tuesday after a\par joint statement from European officials helped the U.S. dollar\par rally.\par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was well off recent record lows against\par the euro and five-year trough against the Japanese yen after\par the head of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and euro zone finance\par ministers said in the joint statement they were unhappy with\par the euro's surge and they were closely monitoring exchange rate\par swings.\par     In Asia, the dollar rallied over 6 won from Monday's\par seven-year low near 1,037 against the South Korean unit. Still,\par the won was a shade stronger against the yen.\par     The Sing dollar was on the firmer side of 1.64 but well off\par last week's six-year peak and the Taiwan dollar retreated\par further from last week's four-year high of 31.96.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thailand's markets opened after a holiday and pushed the\par baht down after thin offshore trading had taken it past 39 per\par dollar to a February high on Monday.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS in Singapore,\par said the stepped-up rhetoric from the Japanese and the\par Europeans had given markets an excuse to book profits on their\par extended dollar-bearish positions. Yet, he did not expect the\par European authorities to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein in the euro.\par  \par     "We seem to be entering a consolidation phase," Baweja\par said.\par     That would also give Asian central banks some breathing\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par space although they would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains continued to be as rapid as it has been in the past two\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months, he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUPIAH, PESO LAGGARDS\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah displayed characteristic lethargy,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holding steady levels around 9,060/9,070 a dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso stayed on the weaker side of 56 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, with markets in Manila on alert after newspaper reports\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that Fitch Ratings was likely to downgrade Philippines debt.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The rupiah and peso prove that it is not just a dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par call, and the balance of payments does matter," Baweja said,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par explaining that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia with the strongest\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par external accounts were rallying the most.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah has been weighed down by worries over how new\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono's fragmented cabinet will\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approve key reforms.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It has not reacted to news that the country would sell\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par another 20 percent of its seventh largest bank, PT Bank Permata\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tbk., this week. That stake is estimated to be worth $120\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0232 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.00         102.32       -0.66\par  Sing dlr        1.6360         1.6347       -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr      32.088         32.070       -0.06\par  Korean won     1042.60        1040.80       -0.17\par  Baht             39.18          39.22       +0.10\par  Peso             56.05          56.02       -0.05\par  Rupiah         9070.00        9060.00       -0.11\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.00         107.31       +4.18\par  Sing dlr        1.6360         1.6978       +3.78\par  Taiwan dlr      32.088         33.978       +5.89\par  Korean won     1042.60        1192.00      +14.33\par  Baht             39.18          39.59       +1.03\par  Peso             56.05          55.49       -1.00\par  Rupiah         9070.00        8410.00       -7.28\par  Rupee            43.60          45.60       +4.58.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c7001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
