\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear.  \b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2004\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 3 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar and the\par Thai baht weakened more than half a percent on Friday, leading\par declines in Asia as authorities increased warnings they might\par sell their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem a two-month rally.\par     The Singapore dollar       , which hit a six-year high\par against the dollar on Wednesday, traded at about 1.6422 per\par dollar. The baht  weakened to 39.37 per dollar, paring\par gains that took it to a seven-month high on Thursday.\par     South Korea must be ready to prevent excessive gains in its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and work with other countries to stem sharp \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves that hurt exporters, President Roh Moo-hyun said at a\par press briefing in London on Thursday.\par     The won        surged 14 percent this year to a seven-year\par high on Thursday, leading gains in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against a\par broadly weakening dollar.\par     Roh's comments resonated among other Asian officials,\par particularly in Japan, who may be preparing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par analysts said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The authorities may be signalling that enough is enough,"\par said Song Seng Wun, economist at G.K. Goh Securities in\par Singapore.\par     "With the holiday season coming up, and liquidity low, they\par may think that this is the best time to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because they\par don't want to waste too much ammunition."\par  \par     South Korea has already \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by buying dollars with\par won last month, data showed this week.\par     UBS expects more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bank of Korea as\par authorities seek to protect the country's biggest companies\par which are also the country's largest exporters.\par     The won        weakened 0.3 percent on Friday to about\par 1,044.30 per dollar. The Taiwan dollar  lost half a\par percent to about 32.15 per dollar.\par     "Considering that the Korean domestic economy is not\par exactly humming along it's not surprising that the authorities\par should be whining about the won's gains," said Song.\par     JAPAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     UBS also expects the Bank of Japan to start dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , for the first time since March, this month, to\par stall the yen.\par     The yen        plunged 1.3 percent to about 103.33 per\par dollar on Friday, coming off a five-year high reached on\par Thursday.\par     The Christmas and year-end holiday season reduces trading,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 making it easier for Asian central banks to reverse the rally  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling relatively light amounts of  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Worries that Asian central banks might slow down the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchase of U.S. treasuries to fund the U.S. deficit were eased  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by data on Thursday showing foreign central banks turned net  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 buyers of U.S. Treasuries in the week ending Dec. 1.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian central banks, packing the world's largest foreign  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, have some of the biggest holdings of U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 treasuries.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculation that some might cut purchases of U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government debt to shift to euro assets was partly responsible  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for the dollar's decline against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers expect the dollar to weaken longer term, but say  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could find some support short term on the strength  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the U.S. economy as reflected by rate increases by the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve this year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Analysts expect the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to increase its\par benchmark rate again at a meeting this month.\par     "People may have underestimated the resilience in the U.S.\par economy," said Song. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the\par day at 0335 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.33         101.98       -1.31\par  Sing dlr        1.6431         1.6317       -0.69\par  Taiwan dlr      32.147         31.990       -0.49\par  Korean won     1044.30        1041.40       -0.28\par  Baht             39.38          39.11       -0.69\par  Peso             56.00          56.08       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9050.00        9015.00  