\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr at 4-yr high, won at 7-yr high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar surged to a\par four-year high on Thursday, outperforming most other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after a plunge in oil prices bolstered the outlook\par for oil-importing Asian economies.\par     The 7.5 percent drop in oil prices in New York on Wednesday\par led overseas investors to buy shares across Asia, pushing up\par the region's benchmark stock indexes and triggering further\par dollar sales by Asian exporters already spooked by a two-month\par plunge in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Taiwan dollar appreciated over 0.7 percent to 31.96 per\par dollar, strengthening beyond 32 per dollar for the first time\par since November 2000. The South Korean won strengthened almost\par half a percent to a new seven-year high of 1,041 per dollar.\par     "Those countries should benefit after the oil prices came\par off sharply," said Ashley Davies, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS\par in Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     UBS expects the Taiwan dollar to appreciate further, along\par with the Indian rupee and the Singapore dollar, because of\par their strong domestic economies which complement strong trade\par surpluses.\par     The Indian rupee surged for a fourth day to a new\par seven-month high against the dollar. The dollar dropped to a\par low of 44.08 rupees in later trades, from 44.41 on Wednesday.\par     The rupee's gains were pared in later deals after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up dollar buying and the securities\par regulator decided to put a cap on investment in local corporate\par debt by overseas institutional investors.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar was trading at about 1.6320 per\par dollar, near a six-year high of about 1.6292 set overnight.\par     The rupee and the Singapore dollar have underperformed the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian rally since the start of October on concerns that the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 central banks would not allow excessive strength in their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which could jeopardise prospects for their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exporters.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht surged half a percent to trade at a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seven-month high of 39.12 per dollar, gaining for a third day,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 as optimism about the economy's growth prospects after the drop  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in oil prices added to Tuesday's better-than-expected exports  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 data.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LOOMS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Christy Tan, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that as Asian exporters dumped their dollars, the region's  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were likely to extend their rally through the end of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That was unless central banks in Japan and South Korea  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 jointly started buying dollars to stem the rally in their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean data released on Thursday showed the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That contrasted with data from Japan that showed the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to stay out of the market despite  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 repeated warnings that it might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the first time  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since March.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're not expecting further gains in the won," said UBS'  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Davies. "We expect the won to hold above 1,000 (per dollar)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 because the government will get into trouble with the large  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 conglomerates if they allow the won to appreciate further."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won has appreciated 14.5 percent against the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year, making it the best performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan dollar and the yen are the next best performers, gaining  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over 6 percent and 5 percent respectively.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS expects the Bank of Japan to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the end of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year to halt the yen's gains. The yen gained on Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to its strongest level against the dollar since March 2000.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0810 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       101.98         102.86       +0.86\par  Sing dlr        1.6317         1.6348       +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr      31.968         32.199       +0.72\par  Korean won     1041.40        1046.00       +0.44\par  Baht             39.11          39.32       +0.54\par  Peso             56.00          56.14       +0.24\par  Rupiah         9015.00        9024.00       +0.10\par  Rupee            44.23          44.41       +0.41 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       101.98         107.31       +5.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6317         1.6978       +4.05\par  Taiwan dlr      31.968         33.978       +6.29\par  Korean won     1041.40        1192.00      +14.46\par  Baht             39.11          39.59       +1.21\par  Peso             56.00          55.49       -0.91\par  Rupiah         9015.00        8410.00       -6.71\par  Rupee            44.23          45.60       +3.09 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vidya Ranganathan; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3841)).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c2005y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
