a local dealer.  \par \par \uc2 For the rest of the session, the U.S. dollar consolidated in the low-S$1.6300s, underpinned by talk that the MAS still had bids placed around the S$1.6300 level, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 From a technical analysis perspective, the U.S. dollar's fall against the Singapore dollar appears to be stronger than expected, as support at S$1.6350 was breached, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 'Downward momentum is picking up again and a clear move below S$1.6300 will likely lead to acceleration lower towards the next support at S$1.6220,' said UOB.  \par \par \uc2 UOB added that it lowered its trailing stop to S$1.6430, and that only a rebound above this level would imply the market had seen a temporary low.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020041202e0c2003h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
