\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 824 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 29 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Monday, led by the Taiwan dollar, on concerns the region's\par central banks may come together and buy dollars to stall a\par two-month rally which has driven some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to multi-year\par highs.\par     The Taiwan dollar weakened 0.2 percent to 32.16 per dollar\par and the Singapore dollar fell as low as 1.6410, before\par recovering some lost ground.\par  \par     The South Korean won pared its losses after weakening as\par much as 0.6 percent in early trading.\par     Some investors took profits, winding down bets for a\par weakening dollar, on the run-up in the won and other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this month.\par     The won has surged nearly 7 percent and the Taiwan dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has appreciated about 4 percent since the end of October,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 beating the less than 3 percent gain in the yen against the  \par \par \uc2 dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Others refrained from further purchases of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 on worries the central banks in Japan, South Korea, Taiwan and  \par \par \uc2 Singapore may not tolerate further gains in their units,  \par \par \uc2 traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The market and the central banks are staring at each  \par \par \uc2 other, trying to call each other's bluff right now," said  \par \par \uc2 Philip Wee, treasury markets strategist at DBS Bank in  \par \par \uc2 Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "We're monitoring for any signs of a possible coordinated  \par \par \uc2 move among Asian central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 South Korean Deputy Finance Minister Chin Dong-soo said the  \par \par \uc2 won was rising faster than other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the  \par \par \uc2 government would coordinate with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the  \par \par \uc2 volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The verbal warnings followed dollar purchases by state-run  \par \par \uc2 banks, which traders said were acting on behalf of the  \par \par \uc2 government.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar has gained the least among the major  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month on concern the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 of Singapore may not tolerate sharp gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 1.3 percent since the end of October.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said there were no indications of  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS on Monday although the market remained  \par \par \uc2 cautious of pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too high.  \par \par \uc2 WON CROSSES  \par \par \uc2 Traders are particularly worried about Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 after the won strengthened against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and the  \par \par \uc2 yen this month.  \par \par \uc2 The won has gained to 10.16 per yen on Monday from about  \par \par \uc2 10.57 per yen at the end of October. The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 has surged to almost 637.5 per Singapore dollar from 673 over  \par \par \uc2 the same period.  \par \par \uc2 "The Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to calm down the markets  \par \par \uc2 for the shorter term," said Mark Cranfield, head of treasury  \par \par \uc2 and capital markets at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg.  \par \par \uc2 "Trading was frantic and truly became reckless last week,"  \par \par \uc2 he said, referring to a 1 percent surge in the won on Friday as  \par \par \uc2 local exporters dumped their dollar receipts on worries that  \par \par \uc2 the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue its decline against the won and  \par \par \uc2 other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders and investors are also watching for further signs  \par \par \uc2 about the global demand for U.S. treasury bills and other  \par \par \uc2 dollar-assets, said Wee at DBS Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks of Japan, China, South Korea and other Asian  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are among the biggest holders of U.S. treasury bills  \par \par \uc2 outside the United States.  \par \par \uc2 Russia indicated earlier this month it plans to boost the  \par \par \uc2 proportion of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves made up by euros  \par \par \uc2 while a Chinese newspaper report on Friday cited a local  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisor saying China may have trimmed its holdings  \par \par \uc2 of U.S. treasuries.  \par \par \uc2 The advisor later said he was only citing U.S. government  \par \par \uc2 data, but the issue continues to worry traders and put pressure  \par \par \uc2 on the dollar over the longer term.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a subject that nobody wants to talk about but is  \par \par \uc2 there at the back of everyone's mind," Cranfield said. "Is Asia  \par \par \uc2 still buying U.S. treasuries?" \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0851 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.07         102.69       -0.37\par  Sing dlr        1.6410         1.6394       -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      32.150         32.095       -0.17\par  Korean won     1046.90        1047.30       +0.04\par  Baht             39.52          39.46       -0.15\par  Rupiah         9010.00        8985.00       -0.28\par  Rupee            44.96          45.03       +0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.07         107.31       +4.11\par  Sing dlr        1.6410         1.6978       +3.46\par  Taiwan dlr      32.150         33.978       +5.69\par  Korean won     1046.90        1192.00      +13.86\par  Baht             39.52          39.59       +0.16\par  Peso             56.10          55.49       -1.09\par  Rupiah         9010.00        8410.00       -6.66\par  Rupee            44.96          45.60       +1.42 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vidya Ranganathan; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3841)).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
