\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Taiwan dollar weaken on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 04:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 29 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Monday, led by the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar,\par after state-run banks stepped in to buy dollars to curb a rally\par that drove regionals to multi-year highs last week.\par     The South Korean won lost as much as 0.6 percent against\par the dollar to 1,053 per dollar in local trades on suspected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , before recovering most of its lost\par ground. The Taiwan dollar weakened 0.3 percent to 32.205 per\par dollar.\par     Government officials in Japan and South Korea have\par threatened to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past month to stem the\par dollar's broad-based slide that drove the won to a 7-year high\par and the Taiwan dollar to a 4-year high last week.\par     South Korea is particularly hurt by the weaker dollar\par because the won has appreciated 10 percent in the past three\par months to outperform other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained 1 percent on Friday as the rally\par triggered sales of dollar receipts by the country's exporters.\par     "The Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needed to calm down the markets\par for the shorter term," said Mark Cranfield, head of treasury\par and capital markets at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg.\par     "Trading was frantic and truly became reckless last week. I\par wouldn't be surprised if the Bank of Japan was in the market\par too."\par     The won also came under pressure after data showed South\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea's industrial production fell a seasonally adjusted 0.9  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent in October from the month earlier. Analysts in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters poll had expected a median rise of 0.7 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While South Korea's current account surplus has tripled in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the first 10 months of this year, export growth has slowed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since the second quarter, dragging on the outlook for the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economy already weakened by a slump in domestic consumer  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 demand.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CHINA FACTOR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar traded at about 1.6385/90, close to a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6-year high.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were weighed down by Chinese Premier  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wen Jiabao's statements on Sunday signalling the country was in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 no rush to revalue the yuan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jiabao said China needed a stable economy and a healthy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 financial system before making changes to the yuan's peg to the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculation that China might soon relax controls over its  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and allow the yuan to trade in a broader band had  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fuelled the rally in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think you can believe (Premier Wen)," said Cranfield.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The bottomline is that China would do only what's important  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for them. It'll never do what the rest of the world wants them  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to do."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cranfield said the dollar was likely to continue on its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakening trend against most major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the longer  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 term.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since the start of this year, the dollar has weakened  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 almost 14 percent against the won, nearly 6 percent against the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan dollar and over 4 percent against the yen as U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 officials voiced concerns about the country's widening current  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 account deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several U.S. Federal Reserve officials have argued that the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shortfall could be met by a drop in the value of the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of major trading partners of the U.S..  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0241 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.86         102.69       -0.17\par  Sing dlr        1.6386         1.6394       +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      32.137         32.095       -0.13\par  Korean won     1047.40        1047.30       -0.01\par  Baht             39.49          39.46       -0.08\par  Rupiah         9005.00        8985.00       -0.22\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.86         107.31       +4.33\par  Sing dlr        1.6386         1.6978       +3.61\par  Taiwan dlr      32.137         33.978       +5.73\par  Korean won     1047.40 