\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-GLOBAL MARKETS-New dollar low caps Tokyo stocks, buoys.  \b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2004\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In SINGAPORE story headlined "New dollar low caps Tokyo\par  stocks, buoys gold" please read in first paragraph ... on\par  Friday ... instead of ... on Thursday ... (corrects day).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A corrected story follows.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a record low against the euro on Friday as traders tested the will of central banks to stop its slide, leaving Tokyo stocks flat on worries about a strong yen and keeping gold near a 16-year high.  \par \par \uc2 Gains in steel makers and other basic industries shares underpinned Asian stock markets, driving a regional index of shares outside Japan to its highest level in nearly 5 years.  \par \par \uc2 "The market remains emboldened that the USD can fall further," said Greg Gibbs, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Asia Royal Bank of Canada Capital Markets. "As it probes the resistance of authorities to accept appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it finds very little."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With trading thinned by the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday on Thursday,\par Tokyo traders beat the dollar down to a record low of $1.3283 per euro\par . The yen  traded near a 5-year high of 102.37 yen        reached in\par London.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Steel producer shares firmed for the second day in a row amid growing evidence of a shortage of the metal among Japanese carmakers and the prospect of higher product prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nippon Steel Corp. (5401.T) climbed 2.4 percent and JFE Steel Corp. (5411.T) rose 2.9 percent after Nissan Motor Co. (7201.T) said the shortage would force it to stop some production.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan, which procures steel from Nippon Steel and JFE, has also asked South Korea's POSCO for emergency supplies. POSCO shares touched a record high and stood 2.9 percent ahead on the day. Nissan fell half a percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average  was flat at 10,897.87. An MSCI index\par of non-Japan shares            climbed 0.42 percent to its highest\par level since March 2000, pushing MSCI's World Index           up 0.3\par percent to a 3-year high.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DRUG MERGER  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Dainippon Pharmaceutical Co. (4506.T) gained 5 percent after agreeing to a merger with the drug unit of Sumitomo Chemical Co. Ltd. (4005.T), up 2.4 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Their gains offset slippage elsewhere on concerns about the effect of yen strength on exports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Hong Kong, shares in state controlled CNOOC (0883.HK) slipped 4.5 percent after it issued a US$850 million convertible bond, a record size for a mainland Chinese firm.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng index rose 0.22 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LCD makers gained in Taiwan on news of production delays at rivals using faulty equipment made by Canon Inc. (7751.T).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AU Optronics (2409.TW), the world's third largest display screen maker, was up 3.64 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The problems with Canon's equipment could slow down the increase in supply, and that is good news. This sector has not had real good news for a long time," said Alvin Teng, assistant research manager at SinoPac Securities.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's benchmark index  rose 0.67 percent, Australia's S&P ASX 200\par      climbed more than 0.2 percent to another record high, while South\par Korea's KOSPI         added 0.91 percent. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Straits Times\par    rose 0.14 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VERBAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOT ENOUGH  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold hovered $1 below a 16-1/4-year high of $452.75 struck in Europe on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was trading at $1.3258 per euro, compared with $1.3270 in very thin, late New York trade, and at 102.55 yen, little changed from New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A repeat of a warning against dollar weakness from Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki, who threatened to take action against sudden moves, had little impact.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's just a matter of when monetary authorities are going to crank up the tone of verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but at this point verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't going to stop the dollar's fall," said Hideaki Furumaya, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Trust and Custody Services Bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even so, the market was looking forward to comments later in the day from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Jean-Claude Trichet, who is due to speak in Rio de Janeiro, along with ECB council member and Spanish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Jaime Caruana.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trichet, who referred to recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements as "brutal" earlier in the month, has become the most vocal European policymaker on dollar weakness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders were expecting market liquidity to remain thin because of the extended U.S. holiday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In such thin trading, many said a fall in the dollar past 102 yen and $1.33 per euro was a real possibility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brent crude oil for January delivery was indicated slightly higher in early Asian trade, bid at $44.71 a barrel, up from up from $44.66 in London. The U.S. NYMEX crude market was closed.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041126e0bq002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
