\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Boosted by China talk, won surges.  \b0\par\par\uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2004\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 25 (Reuters) - Increased speculation of a\par Chinese yuan revaluation boosted Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday,\par taking the South Korean won to a seven-year high, the Taiwan\par dollar to a four-year high and the Sing dollar to fresh\par six-year highs.\par     The Sing dollar        firmed to 1.6395 per dollar, Reuters\par data showed, a level last seen in December 1998, as the\par rallying yen and rising premium on the yuan buoyed Asian\par regionals.\par     Talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the\par Bank of Korea did not deter markets, although a Singapore-based\par trader said dollar/Sing was "quite well supported" around 1.64.\par  \par     Asian regionals were already on a firm footing as the U.S.\par dollar extended a two-month slide to another record low against\par the euro        and 4-=   year lows versus the yen       ,\par undermined by concerns over the U.S. trade deficit.\par     The apparent lack of U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  concern over the dollar's descent\par and the possibility Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might increase euro\par holdings has hurt the dollar this week.\par     The yuan premiums on near-term non-deliverable forwards\par   rose to their highest since October 2003 on talk that\par Beijing would decide on a yuan regime change soon.\par     The speculation was fuelled by research reports that\par suggested a desision on the yuan could be taken at an annual\par Central Economic Work Conference at the weekend.\par     Callum Henderson, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at Standard\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chartered Bank in Singapore, said he'd be surprised if China  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 announced a shift in the yuan policy at the meeting. He expects  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will move only in the first quarter of 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The risk is not zero, but if people are trading on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expectations that China will announce a band widening or a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revaluation on Monday, they are likely to be disappointed,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Henderson said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For over two years markets have speculated China would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 alter its trading band for the yuan, ceding to pressure from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the United States and other industrialised nations that say an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 undervalued yuan gives Chinese exporters an unfair advantage.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The yuan has been kept in a narrow band around 8.28 a\par dollar since late 1997.\par     The one-month yuan NDF premium quoted as high as 720 points\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Thursday, although it eased in later deals. That level  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prices in an appreciation of nearly 1 percent in the yuan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 within a month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GO SLOW   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won             strengthened nearly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a percent to 1,057 per dollar, a level last seen during the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian financial crisis in November 1997, as it shrugged off the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 threat of Bank of Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of buying dollars to cap the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won around 1,060 per dollar on Monday and Tuesday, and the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government has voiced concerns about the won's rise.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Taiwan dollar          rose to 32.18 per dollar, its\par strongest since November 2000.\par     Even the Indonesian rupiah managed small gains, rising to\par levels around 8,960 a dollar.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Deustche Bank, said\par markets need not fear Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "We are in a new regime, a new environment for\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\par     "Increasingly, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be seen as something which\par does not work and which simply subsidises fresh market\par positions."\par     Standard Chartered's Henderson said he would however advise\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trimming some of the long Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positions heading into  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the end of the year, especially in outperformers such as the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won and Taiwan dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Stay long (Asia) in the medium term but start taking some  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 money off the table as we head into the year-end," he said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0820 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.54         103.23       +0.67\par  Sing dlr        1.6394         1.6416       +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr      32.239   