\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  hurts won, baht rises.  \b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 24 (Reuters) - Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled\par the Korean won away from seven-year highs on Wednesday while\par the Thai baht, one of Asia's laggards in the two-month long\par rally against the dollar, rose to a new seven-month high.\par     The threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loomed large in north Asia. Even\par as Russia's proposal to review the share of euros in its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves pushed the euro  to record\par highs, the yen  stalled about half a yen before last\par week's peaks near 102.75 per dollar.\par     The Korean won                   fell as far as 1,068.8 a\par dollar, off a 7-year high of 1,060 hit on Monday and Tuesday,\par after state-run banks were seen buying dollars aggressively.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retained their upward bias.\par     Reuters data showed the Singapore dollar\par strengthened to 1.6420, a new 6-year high, and the Thai baht\par   was quoted at 39.67, its highest since April.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The Taiwan\par  \par dollar          equalled Friday's 3-=   year peak of 32.352 per\par dollar.\par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation in Asia will not occur in a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 straight line. There are already some signs of profit-taking  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and position-squaring, these will likely continue as the year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comes to an end," Vincent Low, head of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at Merrill Lynch, said in a note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Low said some signs of weakness in equities - foreigners  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 turned net sellers of Korean and Taiwan shares this week after  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 being net buyers for most of this month - were among the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 factors that could test authorities' tolerance of stronger  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Authorities in Japan, and by default the rest of Asia, may  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be less willing to tolerate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength if there are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 signs that their economies are not able to withstand tighter  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policies.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Continued signs of equity weakness could be a precursor to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Low said.\par     WON STALLS\par     Traders were not surprised to hear Korean authorities may\par have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein in the won.\par     "The won has outdone even the yen and is too strong\par relative to the region. The Koreans have a case for smoothening\par the won's move," said Philip Wee, a strategist with DBS Bank.\par     The won has risen nearly 5 percent this month, compared\par with the yen's 2 percent, the Taiwan dollar's 3 percent and the\par Singapore dollar's 1 percent gains.\par     The yen-won cross            moved to 10.3 won per yen this\par week from 10.7 in late October, reflecting the won's strength.\par     On Monday, the finance ministry was reported to have asked\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea to take a more aggressive stance on the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . On Wednesday, a Korean business leader said the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 finance ministry had asked firms to moderate their dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 selling.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Merrill's Low said he would exclude the won from any\par long-Asia basket trades.\par     "Given that a short dollar/won trade has done well in 2004\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and that the macro dynamics in Korea - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cutting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates, still-fragile household balance sheets - are somewhat  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 different from the region's norm, we will likely exclude the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won in future Asia baskets," Low said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0812 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.23         103.34       +0.11\par  Sing dlr        1.6416         1.6468       +0.32\par  Taiwan dlr      32.387         32.487       +0.31\par  Korean won     1066.60        1065.70       -0.08\par  Baht             39.67          39.87       +0.50\par  Peso             56.33          56.29       -0.06\par  Rupiah         8980.00        9000.00       +0.22\par  Rupee            45.03          45.04       +0.02\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.23         107.31       +3.95\par  Sing dlr        1.6416         1.6978       +3.42\par  Taiwan dlr      32.387         33.978       +4.91\par  Korean won     1066.60        1192.00      +11.76\par  Baht             39.67          39.59       -0.21\par  Peso      