\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late On Purchase By US Funds; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 07:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was stronger in Asia late Wednesday as U.S. funds used bullish remarks on the baht by Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra as a reason to buy the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices were also higher, mainly due to lower interbank rates and dip-buying interest, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0640 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6431, down from S$1.6465 in Asia late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6420 and S$1.6448 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Given rife speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday to stem the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide to a fresh six-year low of S$1.6414, the U.S. unit kicked off Wednesday's Asian session on a positive note near the mid-S$1.6400 level.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. dollar dropped as low as S$1.6420 in the morning after Thaksin said that the strong baht shouldn't have much adverse effect on Thailand's exports. Thai exporters must adapt to a stronger baht as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to rise further against the U.S. dollar, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "U.S. funds sold dollar-Sing and dollar-baht" on Thaksin's comments, said a Singapore dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Thaksin's comments on the baht may have sparked similar notions among U.S. funds that Singapore authorities may be resigned to a stronger local dollar and won't do much to support the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Early in the afternoon, the U.S. dollar recovered slightly to around S$1.6435 levels on its mild rebound against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen.  \par \par \uc2 For the rest of the week, the U.S. unit is likely to trade in a relatively narrow S$1.6400-S$1.6480 range, United Overseas Bank said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "With the euro struggling above US$1.3100, the U.S. dollar still above Y103.00 and talk of MAS in the market, the dollar-Sing's downside should be limited to S$1.6400 for now," it said. [ 24-11-04 0651GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were mostly higher late Wednesday, aided by an overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys and softer local interbank rates, which keep borrowing costs down, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Late in the local session, the yield on two-year Singapore government bonds was down six basis points at 1.53%. At the longer end of the curve, the 10-year yield fell six basis points to 2.88%, while the 15-year yield shed seven basis points to 3.30%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were mostly lower too, in line with local bond yields.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year swap offer was at 1.71%, down from 1.76% late Tuesday, the five-year swap offer was at 2.39% versus 2.43%, while the 10-year offer fell to 3.09% from 3.15%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 138 basis points from 139 basis points late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 In the interbank market, the overnight rate slipped to 0.1875% from 0.5000% late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change.  \par \par \uc2 Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui and Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 24-11-04 0825GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041124e0bo0008l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
