\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  talk hits South Korean won.  \b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 22 (Reuters) - Suspicion that the Bank of\par Korea had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell won caused the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to trim\par some gains on Monday, while the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also\par curtailed the Taiwan dollar and the Japanese yen.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit fresh multi-year highs on Friday and\par in Monday morning deals after the Group of 20 nations' meeting\par over the weekend failed to address the U.S. dollar's descent.\par     The U.S. unit's drop came on the back of Federal Reserve\par Chairman Alan Greenspan's comments that a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might\par be needed to trim the U.S. current account deficit.\par     The markets had expected the G20 meeting to discuss\par curtailing the dollar's steep fall since October. However, the\par issue was not raised in the group's final communique despite\par calls from European leaders for calm in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par     The euro        was near record highs on Monday but the\par Japanese yen  strayed half a yen off Friday's multi-year\par peak.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean won                   moved up to 1,060\par per dollar, a fresh seven-year high and a level last seen in\par the midst of the 1990s Asian financial crisis. But it soon\par dropped as far as 1,068 per dollar in some local deals on talk\par the Bank of Korea (BOK) bought dollars.\par     A won non-deliverable forwards trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was around 1,063 and it\par spurred the market to push the won down to 1,068 per dollar.\par     There were reports the finance ministry had asked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take a more aggressive role in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market. The head of the Bank of Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par team, Oh Jae-kwon, said the won's gains were excessive.\par  \par     Japan's Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated Japan's\par resolve to act against rapid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par     The Taiwan dollar          retreated from a level of 32.355\par per dollar hit in early trade, within striking distance of\par Friday's levels, the highest since March 2001.\par     The Sing dollar        fell back from 1.6435 a dollar, its\par highest since December 1998.\par     Analysts at ABN AMRO Bank said in a note to clients the\par dollar was likely to be sold in Asia but the wariness over\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would rein the regionals in.\par     "The downside in dollar/Asia is probably intact," said\par Simon Flint, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Bank of America in\par Singapore.\par     "The U.S. prefer a weaker dollar at this point in time and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that chimes with what Alan Greenspan said on Friday. So the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pressure on the dollar is downwards and therefore the pressure  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on dollar/Asia is still downwards."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But regional authorities would increasingly get worried\par about their rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par     "There is no doubt that some Asian authorities are\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 uncomfortable with their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even at present levels and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they are likely to become more aggressive if dollar/Asia  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 continues to fall," Flint said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "You will start getting some resistance at this point in\par time to slow down the appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The Thai baht        which had so far lagged the region\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stayed firm around 39.90 a dollar, having swung to its highest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 levels since early May on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0852 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.22         104.16       +0.91\par  Sing dlr        1.6453         1.6516       +0.38\par  Taiwan dlr      32.479         32.547       +0.21\par  Korean won     1065.30        1068.70       +0.32\par  Baht             39.89          40.16       +0.69\par  Peso             56.27          56.32       +0.09\par  Rupiah         8983.00        8980.00       -0.03\par  Rupee            45.07          45.15       +0.17\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.22         107.31       +3.96\par  Sing dlr        1.6453         1.6978       +3.19\par  Taiwan dlr      32.479         33.978       +4.62\par  Korean won     1065.30        1192.00      +11.89\par  Baht             39.89          39.59       -0.75\par  Peso             56.27          55.49       -1.39\par  Rupiah         8983.00        8410.00       -6.38\par  Rupee            45.07          45.60       +1.16.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041122e0bm006vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
