\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Sing lose steam on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2004\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\par retreated on Wednesday from a 7-year high and the Singapore\par dollar lost ground, after rising to its strongest level in\par almost 5 years, on concern about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying and\par slowing growth.\par     The won backed off its high of 1,089 per dollar reached on\par Tuesday after a senior official said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was ready\par to step in to buy dollars to smooth out the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rally.\par The won has gained 5.5 percent since the start of October.\par     South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed a $7.7 billion rise\par in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves in the first half of November,\par which analysts said indicated increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the won's rally.\par     "We can expect a lot more verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said David\par Simmonds, emerging markets strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland\par in Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "I struggle to make a case for the won going stronger\par because Korean fundamentals ain't that good."\par     The Singapore dollar traded around 1.65 per dollar after\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government said Singapore's economy shrank at a 3.0 percent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par annualised rate in the third quarter of 2004 from the second\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter, as demand for electronics and drugs slowed. The figure\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was deeper than an advanced estimate released in October.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government revised down its forecast for full-year\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic growth to 8-8.5 percent from 8-9 percent and said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there was a risk that microchip exporters could see a "sharp"\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowdown in sales in 2005.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the GDP data matched analysts' expectations, it could\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par curb further gains in the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Joseph Tan,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economist at Standard Chartered Bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Simmonds said further gains in the Singapore dollar against\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar would be determined by gains in other major\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par world \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the euro and the yen and not by the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength of the Singapore economy.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, which guides its\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy through the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , wouldn't want the\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen further because growth is slowing and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the pace of exports is likely to cool in the coming months, he\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Leading indicators for Singapore don't look particularly\par strong," he said.\par     Banks and stock markets in Indonesia are closed this week\par for a Muslim festival.\par     The Taiwan dollar and the Thai baht bucked the declining\par trend among Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because they had lagged the rally\par since the start of October.\par     The Taiwan dollar appreciated to a new 7-month high of\par 32.775 per dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would hit a three-and-half-year\par high if it breaches 32.75 reached on April 13.\par     The Taiwan dollar particularly looks attractive because\par Taiwan's economy was stronger than many of its Asian rivals,\par said Simmonds.\par     "I'd rather be short dollar-Taiwan," he said. "Domestic\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand fundamentals in Taiwan look a bit stronger, inflation\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has picked up." \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.45         105.42       -0.03\par  Sing dlr        1.6501         1.6483       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      32.788         32.819       +0.09\par  Korean won     1091.20        1090.30       -0.08\par  Baht             40.32          40.36       +0.10\par  Peso             56.35          56.36       +0.02 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.45         107.31       +1.76\par  Sing dlr        1.6501         1.6978       +2.89\par  Taiwan dlr      32.788         33.978       +3.63\par  Korean won     1091.20        1192.00       +9.24\par  Baht             40.32          39.59       -1.82\par  Peso             56.35          55.49       -1.52\par  Rupiah         8992.00        8410.00       -6.47\par  Rupee            45.06          45.60       +1.19 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Neil Fullick; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3841)).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041117e0bh003bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
