\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Steady Late Amid MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2004\par 09:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was nearly flat in Asia late Friday after selling by local banks, rumored to have been on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulled it off the early high against the U.S. dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices were almost unchanged in very thin trade ahead of U.S. economic data due out later in the global day and a long weekend in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 At 0715 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6552, almost unchanged from S$1.6550 in Asia late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.6513 and S$1.6569 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore's financial markets were closed for a holiday Thursday and will be shut again Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Despite strong selling by foreign investment banks, the U.S. dollar continued to gain on persistent buying on dips by local banks. It hit the mid-S$1.6500s by the early afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the buying may have been on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore aimed at tempering the renewed U.S. dollar weakness against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At its lowest point of S$1.6513 Friday, the U.S. unit was about 0.6% below its Wednesday high of S$1.6610, and could continue lower in the coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 In a monthly research report, HSBC said it doesn't expect the Singapore dollar, whether measured against its trade-weighted basket or the U.S. dollar, to wane anytime soon even though the island's gross domestic product growth is expected to moderate to around 4.0% next year from an estimated 8.5% to 9.0% in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 That is because the economy will remain close to full capacity, which means MAS will likely keep its stance of seeking a steady and gradual appreciation in the trade-weighted Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The slack in the city-state's economy following the dotcom crash in 2001 has now been absorbed, with unemployment falling to a three-year low of 3.4% in the third quarter of this year, HSBC said. [ 12-11-04 0802GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were mostly flat late Friday in quiet trading before the long weekend and a series of U.S. economic data including October retail sales and September business inventories due later, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the yield on two-year Singapore government bonds was at 1.56% and the 10-year yield was at 3.15%, both unchanged from their previous close Wednesday, while the 15-year yield rose one basis point to 3.59%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were mostly higher near the end of the session.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year swap offer was at 1.73%, up from 1.72% late Wednesday. The five-year swap offer was flat at 2.54%, while the 10-year offer rose to 3.37% from 3.36%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was also steady at 164 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 In the interbank market, the overnight rate was up at 1.2500% from 1.1250% late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and subject to change.  \par \par \uc2 Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ryan Woo [ 12-11-04 0810GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041112e0bc000ew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
