\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -South Korean won near 4-year high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2004\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The South Korean won tested a\par four-year high on Tuesday after data showed strong export and\par record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves while other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par steadied ahead of U.S. presidential elections.\par     The won            ended domestic trading at 1,114.8 per\par dollar, its strongest close since September 2000, and traded at\par 1,114.1 in offshore deals  on speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may hold off cutting interest rates next week after the\par strong trade data and figures showing a rise in core inflation.\par     "The latest figures have given the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a bit of a\par boost," said David Simmonds, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the Royal\par Bank of Scotland.\par     "Export growth stays pretty strong and the trade surplus\par remains extremely large. So there's strong supply of dollars in\par the market.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  That reduces the risk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively in the market."\par     The won has strengthened about 4.5 percent in the past\par three months against the dollar, mirroring similar gains in the\par yen against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     South Korean exporters compete with Japanese and Chinese\par companies in the U.S. and European markets. Analysts say the\par government tries to keep the won's gains in line with gains in\par the yen to keep exports competitive.\par     U.S. ELECTION UNCERTAINTY\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which had posted gains during\par October, were little changed ahead of the U.S. elections that,\par polls suggest, may not throw up a clear winner between\par incumbent President George W. Bush and Democratic contender\par Senator John Kerry.\par  \par     That could lead to a protracted legal wrangle, just as the\par previous election in 2000.\par     "The election uncertainty is weighing on the market," said\par Thio Chin Loo, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BNP Paribas.\par     "The fundamentals still point to a weaker dollar."\par     Record U.S. trade deficits and concerns about an economic\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slowdown in the world's largest economy owing to record high  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 oil prices drove the U.S. dollar last week to its weakest level  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the Singapore dollar in six months and to its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakest in five months against the Taiwan dollar .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Taiwan dollar set a new five-month high of 33.38 per\par U.S. dollar on Tuesday.\par     The Singapore dollar gave up some gains, weakening at one\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 point to 1.6679 per dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has traded within a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 range of 1.66 to 1.6679 per dollar for the last seven days -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unable to rise further on concerns that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent further gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The authority, which conducts monetary policy by guiding  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  within an undisclosed trade-weighted band, has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said it would allow a gradual and modest appreciation of the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb inflationary pressures.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Singapore dollar breaches its April highs of around  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.66 per dollar, it would trade at its strongest level against  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since January 2000.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It has gained 3.3 percent in the past quarter against the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar and it may have some more room for gains before it  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reaches the top end of its trade-weighted band, BNP Paribas'  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thio said. She said the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could strengthen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to 1.65 if the U.S. dollar weakens further against major world  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following the U.S. elections.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0803 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.63         106.39       -0.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6676         1.6643       -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      33.482         33.457       -0.07\par  Korean won     1114.80        1119.00       +0.38\par  Baht             41.07          41.08       +0.04\par  Peso             56.32          56.33       +0.02\par  Rupiah         9100.00        9087.00