\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Clinging to gains ahead of US election.  \b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2004\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The South Korean won steadied\par near its strongest level in four years on Tuesday and other\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held on to October's gains as traders braced\par for an indecisive U.S. presidential election that could hurt\par the dollar.\par     As many as 24 out of 25 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists polled by\par Reuters out of London on Monday expected the dollar to weaken\par against the world's major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if Tuesday's U.S. election\par produced no clear winner and the outcome was prolonged by legal\par wrangles.\par     "If the dollar falls further against the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will get a boost," said Thio Chin Loo,  a\par Singapore-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BNP Paribas.\par     "The fundamentals still point to a weaker dollar."\par     The dollar's weakness in the last week of October, caused\par by concerns of widening U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  trade and budget deficits and a\par economic slowdown due to record high oil prices, drove the\par Singapore dollar  to a six-month high and the Taiwan\par dollar  to a five-month high.\par  \par     The Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a new five-month high of 33.38\par against the dollar on Tuesday.\par     Concerns about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were partly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 responsible for thwarting gains in the South Korean won  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 . The won hit a four-year high around 1,114 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar on Friday but has shed some of those gains in the past  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 two sessions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulators in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia had been few and far between in the past six months,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 indicating they are inclined to let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in line with the dollar's broad-based weakness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's been no heavy-handed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks so far," said Thio. "The kind of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  we saw in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the first quarter is absent."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was a strong case for a further strengthening of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won against the dollar, Claudio Piron, a strategist at J.P.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan, said in a report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This was underscored yesterday by the sturdy October trade  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 performance and still high headline inflation and rising core  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 consumer-price-index growth," Piron said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Piron said the risks of a dollar rebound remained,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 particularly if the U.S. election threw up a clear winner and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that outcome was followed by strong U.S. non-farm jobs data,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 due later this week, and a rise in the U.S. Federal Reserve's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 benchmark interest rate next week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Nevertheless, on the big-picture, longer-term view, we  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would prefer to take the opportunity and establish long Asia  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus U.S. dollar positions," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SING DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar, quoted around 1.6645 per dollar, was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 little changed. It has traded in a range of 1.66 to 1.6679  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar in the last seven trading sessions on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concerns that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS) may  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , by buying U.S. dollars, to prevent further gains in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Singapore dollar breaches its April highs around  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.66 per dollar, it would trade at its strongest level against  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since January 2000.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The MAS, which conducts monetary policy by guiding the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  within its undisclosed trade-weighted band, has said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 it will allow a gradual and modest appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 to curb inflationary pressures.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thio expected the Singapore authorities to let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthen to 1.65 per dollar if the U.S. dollar weakened  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the yen and other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 elections.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0244 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.35         106.39       +0.04\par  Sing dlr        1.6645         1.6643       -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      33.459         33.457       -0.01\par  Korean won     1116.70        1119.00       +0.21\par  Baht             41.04          41.08       +0.10\par  Peso             56.32          56.33       +0.02\par  Rupiah         9087.00        9087.00       +0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.35         107.31       +0.90\par  Sing dlr        1.6645         1.6978       +2.00\par  Taiwan dlr      33.459         33.978       +1.55\par  Korean won     1116.70        1192.00       +6.74\par  Baht             41.04          39.59       -3.55\par  Peso             56.32          55.49       -1.46\par  Rupiah         9087.00        8410.00       -7.45\par  Rupee            45.40          45.60       +0.43.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041102e0b20035z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
