\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won up near 4-year high - others little changed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2004\par 05:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\par approached a four-year high against the dollar on Monday while\par other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steadied after October's gains, as\par uncertainty ahead of the U.S. presidential elections weighed on\par the dollar.\par     The won        was boosted by government data that showed\par South Korea's core inflation rose to a 19-month high in\par October, bolstering expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may hold off\par further interest rate cuts.\par     "The core consumer index is still quite high," said Christy\par Tan, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST Ltd in Singapore. "While the\par trend is still of monetary easing, there's a fifty-fifty chance\par of a change in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy."\par     Korean data showed exports grew a faster-than-expected 20.9\par percent in the year through October, but the increase was the\par slowest in 11 months.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have jumped over the past month, with the\par Singapore dollar  surging to a six-month high and the\par Taiwan dollar  trading near a five-month high last\par week, as concerns about the outlook for the U.S. economy under\par a new administration and record high oil prices weighed on the\par dollar.\par     Tuesday's election is a dead heat with President George W.\par Bush and Democratic contender John Kerry tied nationwide in the\par race for the White House, according to a Reuters/Zogby poll\par released on Sunday.\par  \par     An indecisive election or a legal battle to determine the\par winner will further hurt the dollar, analysts say.\par     But gains in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were curtailed on Monday by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 worries that central banks may buy dollars to keep their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 country's exports competitive against those of their Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rivals.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     A senior South Korean commerce ministry official said on\par Monday a stronger won could hurt the economy's competitiveness.\par     "Although the authorities have allowed the won to\par appreciate, there's caution in the market about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par said Tan.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was little changed around 1.6630/40\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar. Many analysts said it may be close to the top end  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore undisclosed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted band.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which conducts monetary policy by guiding  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  within the band, has said it will allow a gradual  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and modest appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar has strengthened about 3.4 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the U.S. dollar in the past three months. The yen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has gained 5 percent against the dollar in the same  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 period.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's surprise rate rise last week, its first in nine  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 years, also held back Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains as exporters fretted  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that demand from Asia's fastest-growing economy may cool.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei average lost half a percent in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 morning trade, pulling the yen lower against the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0329 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.13         105.97       -0.15\par  Sing dlr        1.6633         1.6630       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      33.438         33.435       -0.01\par  Korean won     1115.70        1119.00       +0.30\par  Baht             41.06          41.02       -0.10\par  Peso             56.32          56.32       +0.01\par  Rupiah         9086.00        9068.00       -0.20\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.13         107.31       +1.11\par  Sing dlr        1.6633         1.6978       +2.07\par  Taiwan dlr      33.438         33.978       +1.61\par  Korean won     1115.70        1192.00       +6.84\par  Baht             41.06          39.59       -3.59\par  Peso             56.32          55.49       -1.46\par  Rupiah         9086.00        8410.00       -7.44\par  Rupee            45.33          45.60       +0.58.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041101e0b10040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
