\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steady on dlr rise,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry.  \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2004\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 27 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par steady to lower on Wednesday, paring some of their recent heavy\par gains as economic data and a stock market recovery boosted the\par U.S. dollar.\par     Traders said fear of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par helped push the Sing dollar  away from a five-year high\par it neared this week and brought the Philippine peso\par closer to an all-time low of 56.45.\par     The Thai baht        fell slightly to 41.05/08 a dollar,\par amid market concern about Thailand's south where almost 80\par Muslims, arrested after Monday's riot, suffocated to death\par while being transported by trucks to army barracks.\par     The Korean won                   and Taiwan dollar\par bucked a general weak trend, with the latter trading flat\par around 33.66-33.70 a dollar.\par     "The major movement last night was in the U.S. stock\par market.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All the top performers of last week, both high-yielders\par and majors, have seen heavy profit-taking," said Philip Wee,\par markets strategist with DBS Bank in Singapore.\par     The Dow Jones industrial average        broke a 5-day\par losing streak with its strongest one-day advance since early\par June.\par     Asian stocks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were expected to be weighed\par down by a rise in the benchmark US light crude  price\par back above $55 a barrel.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WORRY\par     The won hit a fresh four-year high of 1,131 in offshore\par deals, but was seen succumbing to the yen's decline in morning\par trade as traders debated the authorities' tolerance for gains\par in the unit.\par     South Korean officials said on Tuesday monetary policy\par would be kept accommodative, to boost domestic demand, and that\par a weaker dollar would help ease inflationary pressures.\par     Separately, a Bank of Korea official said the won was\par following the yen and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise should not be linked\par to the chances of further rate cuts.\par     "On balance, it would appear that Korean authorities are\par preparing for gradual won appreciation so long as yen/won\par maintains an upward bias and corporate export performance is\par not visibly impaired," Claudio Piron, strategist at JP Morgan,\par said in a note.\par     Markets believe Korean authorities are sensitive about the\par won's competitiveness in export markets, especially against the\par yen.\par     The won had lagged the yen's gains this month, falling to\par 10.68 won per yen on Monday from about 10.28 in late September.\par The cross  was down to 10.58 on Wednesday.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \par  Change on the day at   0149 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.89         106.81       -0.07\par  Sing dlr        1.6662         1.6642       -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      33.713         33.693       -0.06\par  Korean won     1131.60        1133.40       +0.16\par  Baht             41.08          41.02       -0.15\par  Peso             56.39          56.34       -0.09\par  Rupiah         9110.00        9061.00       -0.54\par  Rupee            45.67          45.67       +0.00\par