\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  caps some, rest rise.  \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2004\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 16 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were a\par mixed bag on Thursday as a suspicion central banks were\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  halted rallies in the Sing dollar and the north\par Asians while the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah rose on\par recovering stock markets.\par  \par     Asians started the day slightly weaker as their stock\par markets succumbed to the drop in U.S. stocks on Wednesday.\par     But as Chinese offshore forwards renewed their move to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 price in a greater appreciation of the tightly managed yuan and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 foreigners flocked back to Asian stock markets ,  \par \par \uc2 some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed gains.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah rose as far as 9,010 per  \par \par \uc2 dollar, its highest in two months, as markets positioned for  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains after the presidential elections on Sept. 20.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht's        rise was capped around 41.20, near\par Wednesday's seven-week high of 41.18.\par     "Everyone's buying Asian equities. Seems to be a mix of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bargain-hunting in stocks and the view that one must hold as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 little of fixed income as possible when yields are rising,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said one Singapore-based trader.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also, Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards moved  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to price in a higher premium on the yuan, and that provided  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 another boost to the Asians.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market attention is focused on China ahead of an Oct. 1  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Group of Seven meeting in Washington, to which China has been  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 invited. On Wednesday, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow called  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for accelerated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform in China.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-year NDFs were quoted at 2,800 points, pricing in an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation of 3.5 percent in the yuan in a year. The yuan is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 effectively pegged around 8.28 per U.S. dollar.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 But the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and in some cases suspicion of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying capped some of the regionals.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Sing dollar stayed between 1.6890 and 1.69 a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, unable to re-visit this week's four-month high near  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.6880.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Asian central banks were out yesterday, putting a steady  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hand on things," said David Simmonds, markets strategist with  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Royal Bank of Scotland.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Secondly, the dollar rallied a bit on some second-tier\par data," he said.\par     "It's no surprise to see dollar/Asia better bid," he said,\par although he added that the rise had been limited.\par     Analysts said there was also selling of the Sing against\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its trading partners by funds speculating the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had appreciated to the highest end of the undisclosed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted band authorities manage it in.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar held between 33.80 and 33.90 a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar and the Korean won             fell to 1,147 but\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 returned soon to straddle 1,145 for a fourth day.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to follow the rest of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 region higher this week amid suspicion their central banks were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 active in the market to prevent large moves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian rupee was forced off two-month highs  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 near 45.70 on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reported to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be making enquiries. On Thursday, it was pushed closer to 46 by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar-buying by state-owned banks.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0800 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.71         109.44       -0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.6893         1.6876       -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      33.831         33.811       -0.06\par  Korean won     1145.70        1144.10       -0.14\par  Baht             41.30          41.28       -0.05\par  Peso             56.18          56.09       -0.16\par  Rupiah         9055.00        9100.00       +0.50\par  Rupee            45.96          45.84       -0.25\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.71         107.31       -2.19\par  Sin