\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rally pauses on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2004\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 16 (Reuters) - Suspicion that Asian central\par banks were \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow rallies in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par a decline in equity markets weighed on regional units on\par Thursday, halting their recent gains to multi-month highs.\par     The U.S. dollar was a bit stronger after an upbeat U.S.\par manufacturing report and ahead of a Federal Reserve policy\par meeting next week.\par  \par     Even so, the Sing dollar, at around 1.69 a dollar, was only\par marginally off this week's four-month high near 1.6880.\par     The Thai baht slipped from the previous day's seven-week\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  high around 41.18 a dollar to 41.25/27 and the Indonesian   \par \par \uc2  rupiah appeared to have lost the upward momentum that took it   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The rupiah edged down below 9,100 per dollar, having\par weakened from close to 9,050 on Wednesday.\par     The Taiwan dollar held between 33.80 and 33.90 a dollar and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Korean won straddled 1,145 for a third day. These two\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to follow the rest of the region higher this\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week amid suspicion their central banks were active in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market to prevent large moves.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indian rupee was forced off two-month highs near 45.70\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reported to be making\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enquiries.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Asian central banks were out yesterday, putting a steady\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hand on things," said David Simmonds, markets strategist with\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Secondly, the dollar rallied a bit on some second-tier\par data," he said.\par     "It's no surprise to see dollar/Asia better bid," he said,\par although he added that the rise had been limited.\par     Analysts expect that the central banks want to prevent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rapid movements but at the same time would like to see some\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation to fight rising inflation in Asia,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par especially from imported oil.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A lot of market attention was focused on China ahead of an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Oct.1 Group of Seven meeting in Washington, to which China has\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been invited. On Wednesday, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par called for accelerated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform in China.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards have moved to price\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a higher premium on the yuan this week, which means a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par greater appreciation.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One-year NDFs were quoted at 2,700 points, pricing in an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation of over three percent in the yuan in a year. The\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yuan is effectively pegged around 8.28 per U.S. dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "China NDFs are still reasonably well-offered. And the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direction for Asians depends on to what extent we see further\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows into regional equity markets as well," Simmonds said.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.89         109.44       -0.41\par  Sing dlr        1.6892         1.6876       -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      33.823         33.811       -0.04\par  Korean won     1145.70        1144.10       -0.14\par  Baht             41.25          41.28       +0.07\par  Peso             56.12          56.09       -0.04\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9100.00       -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.89         107.31       -2.35\par  Sing dlr        1.6892         1.6978       +0.51\par  Taiwan dlr      33.823         33.978       +0.46\par  Korean won     1145.70        1192.00       +4.04\par  Baht             41.25          39.59       -4.04\par  Peso             56.12          55.49       -1.11\par  Rupiah         9115.00        8410.00       -7.73\par  Rupee            45.84          45.60       -0.53.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040916e09g003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
