\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Southeast Asians at multi-month peaks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2004\par 04:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par extended their rallies to multi-month peaks on Wednesday,\par buoyed by surging stock markets, foreign portfolio inflows and\par the seeming absence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb gains.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        firmed through another key\par level at 1.69 per dollar in offshore deals to hit fresh\par four-month highs near 1.6880, despite concern the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary\par authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the Sing rose too rapidly against\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of trading partners.\par     The Thai baht        and the Indonesian rupiah        were\par both at seven-week highs, hitting 41.18 and 9,050 per dollar\par respectively in morning deals.\par     Major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had little influence on the firming trend\par in these regionals, with the dollar and yen caught in tight\par ranges after data showed the U.S. current account deficit\par surged to a record in the second quarter and retail sales fell\par in August.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Markets are waiting for a Federal Reserve policy meeting\par next week, expecting U.S. rates will be raised again.\par     Analysts said the interest to buy the Asians was gathering\par pace, evidenced in the return of foreign capital to the region\par and stock markets hitting new highs.\par     Moreover, there was speculation that the authorities had\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been encouraging the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation in India, Thailand\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , through either suspected dollar sales or by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par refraining from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupee  hit a two-month high on Tuesday and has\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par risen one percent in a week, driven mainly by speculation that\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the authorities wanted a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fight rapidly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising prices. Annual wholesale price inflation is over eight\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bhanu Baweja of UBS said it was extremely interesting that\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Reserve Bank of India had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the rupee\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets in the past two days "not only because the move was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharp, but also because most of these inflows have been driven\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by onshore-offshore arbitrage, which the RBI has historically\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par frowned upon".\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the RBI also had difficulty soaking up the domestic\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds released through dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , because of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the high inflation and because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not want\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yields to rise.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT CATCHING UP\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baweja said the baht, which has been an underperformer in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the region this year, was likely to benefit from government\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spending on the economy and markets ahead of elections early in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2005.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "While the BoT (Bank of Thailand) have not come in to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact the value of the baht either way, we believe the BoT\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par does regard baht as unfairly weak due to temporary factors such\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the bird flu and the problems in the Southern Thailand that\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have undermined confidence in the Thai economy," Baweja wrote\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a note.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If a stronger stock market was to push the baht somewhat\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger, we don't think the BoT would stand in the way,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par especially as they don't see equity inflows as interest rate\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the Korean won             was virtually\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unchanged and the Taiwan dollar  slightly higher, with\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets suspecting the authorities in these two countries were\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par controlling the movements in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0229 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.68         110.01       +0.30\par  Sing dlr      