\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr up, Korea holds rates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2004\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained on\par Thursday after the dollar's momentum was checked by the\par cautious optimism of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan,\par with the Singapore dollar reaching two-month highs.\par     The dollar weakened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after markets\par interpreted Greenspan's testimony as casting some doubt on the\par extent of expected rate rises later in the year.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar and the north Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  led the\par region's gains, as they have through this month.\par     The Bank of Korea held rates steady at a record low after a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  policy meeting on Thursday. Economists had expected   \par \par \uc2  inflationary pressures would prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave   \par \par \uc2  policy steady after last month's surprise cut, but the market   \par \par \uc2  was wary of being caught out again.   \par \par \uc2  After the decision the South Korean won  hit   \par \par \uc2  1,146.0 per dollar, its highest in local trade since April, but   \par \par \uc2  pulled back towards 1,147. The won's gains took it to levels   \par \par \uc2  where the market has been wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar  headed towards 1.6950 per   \par \par \uc2  dollar in morning trade, a break of which would take it to its   \par \par \uc2  highest levels since May, but edged back as the market wondered   \par \par \uc2  about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's tolerance for   \par \par \uc2  further gains.   \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has gained about one percent against   \par \par \uc2  the dollar so far this month, and analysts estimate it is in   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The MAS targets the trade-weighted Sing in an undisclosed\par band against an undisclosed basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS, said the level of\par the Singapore dollar was not a concern, but said the MAS might\par be a little worried about the speed of the move.\par     "They might come in and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in bits and pieces just\par to slow the market down through key technical levels," Baweja\par said. "I think they have already done that actually."\par     The MAS adopted a tightening bias in April when it said it\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would allow the trade-weighted Sing to rise gradually. Baweja\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimated that the trade-weighted Sing was about two percent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the top of this gradually rising band.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's massive room to the upside and all you need is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger data on the real economy and inflation and you will\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue to go higher," he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We maintain a long Sing dollar against the basket trade."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the Singapore dollar rallied, other Southeast Asian\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were stuck near familiar levels, albeit slightly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger on the day.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  was sitting just above 56.00 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, which has proved solid resistance since late August.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  was holding close to 41.60 per dollar, a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level it has traded around for two weeks.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  fell to near 9,400 per dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week, its lowest since the first round of presidential\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par voting in early July, but has traded around 9,280 per dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Wednesday, the governor of the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said he expected the rupiah to strengthen after the Sept. 20\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presidential election.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0222 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.21         109.49       +0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.6961         1.6988       +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr      33.884         33.914       +0.09\par  Korean won     1146.80        1149.50       +0.24\par  Baht             41.59          41.64       +0.12\par  Peso             56.02          56.10       +0.13\par  Rupiah         9281.00        9266.00       -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.21         107.31       -1.74\par  Sing dlr        1.6961         1.6978       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      33.884         33.978       +0.28\par  Korean won     1146.80        1192.00       +3.94\par  Baht             41.59          39.59       -4.82\par  Peso             56.02          55.49       -0.95\par  Rupiah