\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Oil, yen, equities weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2004\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By John Mair\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\par   and Taiwan dollar          fell to one-week lows on\par Friday as regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  struggled with a record oil\par price, a weakening yen and falling equity markets.\par     The Thai baht        held just above 41.50 per dollar, last\par week's 11-month low, for a third day. It has stalled ahead of\par its low on talk that the Bank of Thailand is checking prices\par and placing some buy orders.\par     The Singapore dollar        was also weaker, but resisting\par a fall through 1.7250 per dollar. That level has held this week\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the Sing dollar fell towards 1.73 last week.\par     Further losses in the yen       , which hit one-week lows\par near 111.90 per dollar, could drive Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower.\par However, the market was expected to range trade ahead of the\par U.S. payrolls data for June later on Friday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     There was support from the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fall through support.\par     "For today, everyone is just waiting for tonight's number,\par after which we'll be looking at what Greenspan is going to do,"\par DBS Bank market strategist Philip Wee said.\par     The market has factored in a rise of 200,000 to 250,000 for\par the payrolls data. The figure will help shape expectations for\par U.S. rate rises through the end of 2004.\par     Oil prices        rose to $44.73 per barrel, the highest\par since oil futures were launched on the New York Mercantile\par Exchange in 1983.\par     Asia imports most of its oil, and the high prices have\par raised concerns that inflation and growth will be adversely\par affected.\par     The higher oil prices also spooked U.S. equity markets,\par which fed through to Asian markets on Friday.\par     Already under pressure from a downgrading of the technology\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sector and slowing investment flows, the prospect of slower\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par global growth hitting demand for Asian exports added to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional equity worries.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The stock market is important for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region so\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Philippine peso        went against the trend,\par strengthening to a one-month high of 55.66 per dollar.\par     Wee, who is cautiously optimistic on the peso, said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore investors were focusing on the long-term structural\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook rather than day-to-day data. This was creating an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par arbitrage opportunity that had led to some demand for the peso,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was an expectation that after her victory in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent presidential election, Gloria Macapagal Arroyo will\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deliver on her promises of reforms, including reining in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     One test would be the planned $4 billion to $5 billion\par privatisation of assets of the National Power Corp. (Napocor).\par     "Basically there's a sense that in her first 100 days we\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might see some success in terms of selling off one of the units\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Napocor, and that would send a positive signal," Wee said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0205 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.61         110.82       -0.71\par  Sing dlr        1.7225         1.7206       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      34.168         34.155       -0.04\par  Korean won     1166.20        1163.10       -0.27\par  Baht             41.46          41.45       -0.02\par  Peso             55.66          55.78       +0.22\par  Rupiah         9187.00        9160.00       -0.29\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.61         107.31       -3.85\par  Sing dlr        1.7225         1.6978       -1.43\par  Taiwan dlr      34.168         33.978       -0.56\par  Korean won     1166.10        1192.00       +2.22\par  Baht             41.46          39.59       -4.52\par  Peso             55.66          55.49       -0.31\par  Rupiah         9187.00        8410.00       -8.46\par  Rupee            46.36          45.60       -1.64.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040806e0860007r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
