\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down Late Following Overnight USD Strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2004\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was lower late Thursday in Asia, hurt by the U.S. dollar's surge against the yen in New York trading overnight.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were barely changed, as players kept to the sidelines ahead of U.S. jobless data later in the global day.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0700 GMT, the U.S. unit was quoted at S$1.7242, up from S$1.7231 around the same time Wednesday. The U.S. dollar started the Asian day around S$1.7264 and kept to a range of S$1.7240 to S$1.7286, as its rally against the yen lost momentum during Asian hours.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar climbed to its highest level in nearly two months against the yen as traders viewed a surge in oil prices Wednesday as positive for the U.S. unit, offsetting disappointment over a U.S. durable goods report that showed orders rose 0.7% in June, well short of the consensus for a 1.5% gain.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0700 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at Y111.63, slightly down from its late New York level of Y111.71.  \par \par \uc2 Movements in the U.S. dollar against the Singapore unit "very much depended on external factors such as dollar-yen (trading) and how the dollar is faring against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer said of Thursday's trading.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, United Overseas Bank said in its daily technical commentary there's no change to its bullish outlook on the U.S. dollar against its local counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 "While S$1.7300 is a formidable resistance, a move above this level is anticipated for an acceleration toward the target at S$1.7400," the bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Putting a cap on the U.S. dollar were fears of further steps by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local unit.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar Wednesday was a "reminder" that the mild appreciation exchange rate policy is still very much in effect, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi said.  \par \par \uc2 In April, Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened monetary policy to allow a "modest and gradual appreciation" of the Singapore dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ 29-07-04 0713GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 There was light selling of Singapore government bonds midafternoon Thursday due to caution ahead of U.S. jobless claims data due later in the global day.  \par \par \uc2 A trader cited the potential for surprises, given recent volatility in the weekly data.  \par \par \uc2 The latest consensus is for a small increase of 4,000 in the number of first-time jobless claims in the week ended July 24, according to the latest Dow Jones-CNBC poll.  \par \par \uc2 Late Thursday in Asia, the yield on the new two-year Singapore government bonds was at 1.44% against 1.42% at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on 10-year bonds was at 3.55% versus 3.51%, while the 15-year yield was at 3.96% from 3.94% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were higher. The two-year swap offer was at 1.68%, up from 1.63% late Wednesday. The five-year swap was at 2.68% against 2.64% previously, while the 10-year swap was at 3.70% compared with 3.65%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was steady at 202 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The interbank overnight rate rose to 0.8125% from 0.6250%.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change.  \par \par \uc2 Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Kevin Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com [ 29-07-04 0812GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040729e07t000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
