\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Supported by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2004\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 29 (Reuters) - A suspicion that Asian\par central banks, many of which are believed to have sold dollars\par this week, were \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the markets on Thursday limited\par losses in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite a weaker Japanese yen.\par     Most of the regionals fell in offshore deals after U.S.\par economic optimism boosted the dollar and pushed the yen\par to fresh six-week lows.\par  \par     Their recovery in early Asian trading suggested the central\par banks were once again defending their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     They said central banks in Taiwan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , India and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia appeared to have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because local  \f28 \par \par \uc2 banks, which are thought to act on their behalf, had supplied  \par \par \uc2 dollars.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The way the offers (of dollars) are coming in this morning\par ... huge offers in the six-month (forwards) in Taiwan, offers\par at 1.7260 in Sing ... I think they are \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said one\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -based trader.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        dropped to near 1.73 in\par offshore deals, its lowest since mid-May, before rebounding to\par Wednesday's levels near 1.7250.\par     The Taiwan dollar          hit a fresh eight-month low of\par 34.27 at the open and then scaled back losses to 34.16/18.\par     The Thai baht        briefly touched a new low since August\par 2003 near 41.50 before paring losses.\par     Traders said the upcoming Thai holiday on Monday was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 causing markets to offload dollars, even though the Bank of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula showed no discomfort  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in remarks made on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Pridiyathorn said the weak baht would not hurt the economy\par and was on account of the U.S. dollar's broader gains.\par     The Korean won                   found support at 1,170 in\par offshore deals and was a shade firmer.\par     UBS strategist Bhanu Baweja said he would sell the won and\par buy the Sing dollar, betting that Singapore's relative economic\par strength would boost its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "It also stacks up well from a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 perspective in that the MAS has been selling U.S. dollars while  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea has been buying dollars to keep the won  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 competitive," he said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0225 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.57         111.33       -0.22\par  Sing dlr        1.7251         1.7238       -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr      34.171         34.199       +0.08\par  Kore