\par\par \b \uc2 Asian central banks step in as  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  trip up.   \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2004\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 28 (Reuters) - Asian central banks appear\par to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets this week after a\par three-month lull, but this time they have been buying their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against a resurgent U.S. dollar, traders say.\par     Central banks in India, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Taiwan, Thailand and\par Indonesia are all suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as some of their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit lows for the year against the dollar this week.\par     That represents a change in tack after the heavy\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  they conducted through all of 2003\par and the first few months of 2004, boosting their combined\par foreign reserves to over $2 trillion.\par  \par     Traders cited dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in India, where\par the rupee hit a fresh one-year low of 46.35/40 on Wednesday.\par     The Taiwan dollar has shed about 1.5 percent in less than\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three weeks and on Wednesday hit 33.23, its lowest in eight   \f28 \par \par \uc2 months. Traders in Singapore said they had heard that the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered U.S. dollars in onshore markets above   \par \par \uc2 34.20.   \par \par \uc2 Expectations of higher yields in a rebounding U.S. economy,   \par \par \uc2 weakness in technology stocks and diminishing interest in the   \par \par \uc2 once-popular Chinese yuan revaluation trade seemed to be   \par \par \uc2 driving foreign funds out of Asia, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 But they felt that policy makers might be reacting too   \par \par \uc2 quickly, given they had been battling strength in their   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a couple of years, until April.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Some of them are hypersensitive at this moment in time,"\par said Claudio Piron, a strategist with Standard Chartered Bank.\par     "And it seems to be a combination of where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 are in historical terms, where they are in their trade-weighted   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 baskets and also in terms of managing inflationary   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expectations."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLICY DILEMMA   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Piron said the Thai baht's two percent slide in two weeks   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had taken it to its lowest levels historically in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted terms. The baht hit 41.45, its weakest since   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 2003, on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said the weak baht would not hurt the economy, traders   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suspected the authorities would sell dollars if there were   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 further losses.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Similarly, analysts said it was reasonable for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary   \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore (MAS) to worry if the Sing dollar moved   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 too far to the weaker side of the trade-weighted band it is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 managed in, particularly after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April it wanted to tighten policy by guiding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 higher.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local banks in Singapore were seen buying their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 this week, spurring suspicion they were acting on behalf of the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MAS.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     South Korean markets have been baffled by conflicting\par statements from policy makers.\par     More than any country in the region, South Korea is faced\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with the dilemma of whether to continue with a policy of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 boosting exports through a cheap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , despite the risk of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher imported inflation from rising oil and commodity prices.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In Korea, they are getting a bit more sensitive in terms   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of price expectations and some of the inflationary pressure,"   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Piron said. "Some of the growth picture has started to fade,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but they don't want price inflation to also deteriorate."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nonetheless, analysts said inflation was still benign in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia and central banks might be acting to curb market   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 volatility rather than signalling a shift in policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040728e07s001rv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
