\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fears limit losses.  \b0\par\par\uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2004\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 27 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on\par Tuesday, some to new lows for the year, as foreign investors\par kept up their liquidation of Asian assets though the fear of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by local central banks lent some support.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        fell as far as 1.7235 before\par returning to the firmer side of 1.72 on heavy sales of U.S.\par dollars by local banks that markets suspected were acting on\par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        hit a three-week low of 9,150\par per dollar before rebounding as Bank Indonesia said it had not\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but would do so if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  became too volatile.\par  \par     The Philippine peso        rose slightly from an early\par level of 56.135, its lowest in a week.\par     The U.S. dollar gave up some of the gains it made against\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the yen and European majors as markets waited for U.S. GDP and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 consumer confidence data to confirm Federal Reserve Chairman  \par \par \uc2 Alan Greenspan's bullish testimony on the U.S. economy last  \par \par \uc2 week. That too provided the region some relief.  \par \par \uc2 "Inasmuch as Asian central banks are concerned about export  \par \par \uc2 competitiveness implied by softness in equities worldwide, they  \par \par \uc2 are unlikely to tolerate excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness either,  \par \par \uc2 due to supply-side inflation pressures," Philip Wee, a  \par \par \uc2 strategist with DBS Bank, said in a note to clients.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't expect runaway depreciation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Still, traders said the early losses showed foreigners were  \par \par \uc2 still pulling their money out of Asian stocks and  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , partly because of rising yields in the United  \par \par \uc2 States and because of waning expectations of a revaluation of  \par \par \uc2 the tightly controlled Chinese yuan .  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar slipped to 34.16, a fresh low  \par \par \uc2 for 2004, and the Thai baht fell to 41.25 a dollar, its  \par \par \uc2 lowest since August 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Wee said the baht was the most vulnerable because Thailand  \par \par \uc2 ranked second in the region in its exposure to the risks of  \par \par \uc2 oil, the yen and stocks. The Taiwan dollar was sensitive to  \par \par \uc2 movements in its stock market, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Asian markets have also been pressured by the fall in the  \par \par \uc2 prices of U.S. technology stocks. The technology-packed Nasdaq  \par \par \uc2 Composite Index posted its lowest close since last  \par \par \uc2 October and the Philadelphia Stock Exchange's semiconductor  \par \par \uc2 index fell to an 11-month low on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     UBS published data showing the Asia-Pacific region lost a\par net $346 million of foreign money in the week to July 23.\par     South Korea's stocks have declined 20 percent while\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's stock market has lost about 23 percent since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mid-April.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0759 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.65         109.74       +0.08\par  Sing dlr        1.7195         1.7200       +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      34.150         34.098       -0.15\par  Korean won     1164.70        1161.30       -0.29\par  Baht             41.15          41.15        0.00\par  Peso             56.01          56.08       +0.12\par  Rupiah         9080.00        9120.00       +0.44\par  Rupee            46.26          46.27       +0.02\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.65         107.31       -2.13\par  Sing dlr        1.7195         1.6978       -1.26\par  Taiwan dlr      34.150         33.978       -0.50\par  Korean won     1164.70        1192.00       +2.34\par  Baht             41.15          39.59       -3.80\par  Peso             56.01          55.49       -0.93\par  Rupiah         9080.00        8410.00       -7.38\par  Rupee            46.26          45.60       -1.44.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040727e07r0015e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
