\par\par \b \uc2 BC-MARKETS-ASIA- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1).  \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2004\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , June 28 (Reuters) - Fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and weak equity markets pushed the Korean won off\par 11-week highs on Monday, while trading was quiet in the rest of\par Asia as markets positioned for a U.S. policy meeting this week.\par     The won                   pulled back from an offshore peak\par near 1,148 per dollar, its highest since mid-April, to hit\par 1,152, even after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said authorities\par respected free movements of the exchange rate.\par     Other regionals kept to narrow ranges, yielding a bit of\par ground to the U.S. dollar as it recovered from last week's lows\par ahead of the Fed's two-day rate-setting meeting from Tuesday.\par     The Singapore dollar        came off Friday's peaks near\par 1.7030 per U.S. dollar to fall as far as 1.71 and the Thai baht\par   weakened from 40.75 to 40.95.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the won's rise last week beyond the sensitive\par 1,150 per dollar level had taken it "back into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par territory."\par     "Equity markets are generally softer. And there is a\par feeling that the won has outperformed some of the other\par regionals recently, notably the Taiwan dollar, and that Bank of\par Korea is keeping a daily close watch," said David Simmonds,\par markets strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland.\par  \par     The won has rallied nearly four percent since mid-May,\par placing it among Asia's best performers this year.\par     RANGE-BOUND\par     Barring the won, most \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were little changed. The\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine peso remained on the weaker side of 56 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, in a narrow band around 56.10/15 while the Indonesian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rupiah moved in a band of 9,400 to 9,420.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets expect the Fed to raise interest rates by a quarter  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percentage point to 1.25 percent on Wednesday, but analysts  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suspect traders would tread carefully until the risk of a more  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 aggressive tightening eased.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Asia is going to remain relatively range bound with  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 corporate demand to buy dollars before the month-end probably  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 being the major flow driver and some moderate interest to sell  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar/Asia from investors," said Peter Redward, Deutsche  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still with markets having priced in the 25 basis points  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rise in U.S. rates, traders would focus more on upcoming data  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in Japan and South Korea and, more keenly, the jobs and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 manufacturing data out of the United States, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0823 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.85         107.63       -0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.7078         1.7074       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      33.751         33.680       -0.21\par  Korean won     1152.40     