\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rise as dlr wobbles, Fed worry ease.  \b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2004\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 25 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led a\par rally in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday as the U.S. dollar\par struggled near multi-week lows against the yen and euro.\par     The won            rose to 1,148.7 per dollar, its highest\par since April 14, before pulling back slightly on fears\par authorities might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the rise, dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        rose by about a cent to 1.7039\par per U.S. dollar, a level last traded on June 9 and about two\par cents above Tuesday's one-month low.\par     The Thai baht        hit 40.79, its highest since June 14,\par and the Taiwan dollar  saw 33.595 per dollar, its\par strongest in more than a week.\par     The Philippine peso       , which hit a record low earlier\par this month, strengthened past 56 per dollar for the first time\par since June 16. However, it unwound those gains in afternoon\par trade.\par  \par     "This is a typical relief rally," said Philip Wee,\par strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Weak data, violence in Iraq, and bomb attacks in Turkey\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of a visit by U.S. President George W. Bush saw markets\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell the dollar on Thursday. It managed to stay off lows hit in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par New York but remained under pressure on Friday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the price action reflected markets were\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par becoming comfortable with an expected rise in U.S. rates next\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week. That was a bigger factor than the violence, they said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. Federal Reserve will hold a policy meeting on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday and Wednesday and is expected to vote for a 25 basis\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par point increase in its key rate, which stands at one percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wee said the fall in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since April appeared\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to have reflected three big risks: rising U.S. interest rates,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We have faced our worst fears and, come to think of it,\par things don't look as bad they did a few weeks back," he said.\par    Wee said the U.S. was likely to raise rates at a measured\par pace, oil prices were off their two-decade highs, and a hard\par landing was not expected for the Chinese economy.\par     BEYOND FED\par     With the markets having fully priced a policy tightening in\par the U.S., many analysts expect concerns about funding the\par country's large current account deficit to weigh on the dollar.\par     Claudio Piron, head of Standard Chartered's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore, said rising inflation in Asia would dampen the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par desire of the region's central banks to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weak and use stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tighten monetary\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Asian policy makers could opt for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offset rising inflationary pressures rather than allowing\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates to rise," Piron said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That argument has already come in focus in Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said investors were taking a closer look at the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after Wednesday's consumer\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par price index showed annual inflation of two percent - the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steepest since December 2000.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore tightened policy in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April, citing the risk of a strong economic recovery stoking\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation. Analysts believe the CPI numbers would reinforce\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that stance.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  targets the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  within an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par undisclosed trade-weighted band. In April it said it would\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allow a gradual strengthening of the trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close  Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.63       107.90         +0.25\par  Sing dlr      1.7074       1.7134         +0.35\par  Taiwan dlr    33.680       33.707         +0.08\par  Korean won   1149.80      1155.70         +0.51\par  Baht           40.84        40.90         +0.15\par  Peso           56.10        56.04         -0.08\par  Rupia