\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steady but risks remain.  \b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2004\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, May 27 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steadied on\par Thursday after recent volatile trade but investors remain\par nervous about a choppy U.S. dollar, high oil prices and the\par threat of terror attacks.\par     Oil prices        fell from near 21-year highs on Wednesday\par but there are concerns high prices would persist until the end\par of June, when the United States is expected to hand over power\par in Iraq to a local administration.\par     The dollar was also hit by weaker-than-expected U.S. data\par and news reports on Wednesday suggesting U.S. officials had\par information about terror attacks planned in the summer.\par     With the yen        stuck between 111.40 and 112 a dollar,\par the Singapore dollar  initially fell to the weaker side\par of 1.71 and then rallied to 1.7060, a three-week high.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won                   caught up with the\par regional appreciation after a market holiday on Wednesday,\par opening domestic trade sharply up at a three-week high close to\par 1,170 per dollar and creating a big gap on the dollar/won\par chart.\par     "It is very difficult. When you have security issues in the\par U.S., the possibility of higher volatility in oil prices until\par the end of next month, those factors are going to mean that\par upside potential for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not that significant," said\par Robert Rennie, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Westpac Bank,\par Sydney.\par     Investors would be unwilling to commit fresh capital to\par Asian assets, and those flows had been the prime drivers of\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains this year, he said.\par  \par     "If for any reason we see the situation in Iraq resolved,\par the value in Asia will become much more compelling," he said.\par     In Thursday's trading, the Indonesian rupiah        was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 still under some pressure from liquidation of positions by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 foreigners and stop-loss trades. It hit 9,300 per dollar,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 edging closer to Tuesday's 19-month trough of 9,350.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso barely moved, staying near the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 56 per dollar level as an official counting of presidential  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 election votes got underway. Leaked unofficial results showed a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 narrow victory for incumbent Gloria Macapagal Arroyo.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PICK SING DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rennie said the Sing dollar and the Korean won offered the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 best value in the region, based on a ranking system that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 included macroeconomic factors, sensitivity to oil prices,  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, said the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was on the verge of an uptrend. The worry  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China might slow sharply had moderated and Singapore shares  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had outperformed other markets in the recent wave of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 equity selling, he said. Besides, risk aversion was easing, he  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In fundamental terms the Singapore story remains a good  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one," he said, referring to a deepening economic recovery,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 especially in manufacturing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore said it was tightening  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy in early April. The MAS conducts its policy through a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted Sing dollar basket, guiding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to tighten policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Baweja said the Singapore dollar had lost 1.4 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against that trade-weighted basket since the policy was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tightened.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "MAS' policy bias, which is executed through the exchange  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rate, together with our fundamental negative view on the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar means we see U.S. dollar/Sing dollar as a sell."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In addition, short-term factors that had kept the Sing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar under the cosh seem to be abating now."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0351 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.48         111.43       -0.04\par  Sing dlr        1.7059         1.7096       +0.22\par  Taiwan dlr      33.490         33.510       +0.06\par  Korean won     1171.60        1179.00       +0.63\par  Baht             40.73          40.70       -0.07\par  Peso             55.94          55.97       +0.05\par  Rupiah         9295.00        9245.00       -0.54\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par 