\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Tone stronger, but moves limited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, March 29 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held a\par stronger tone without actually moving too far on Monday as the\par market debated whether or not Japan had ended its policy of\par massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and political tensions eased in Taiwan.\par     A weekend report in a British newspaper that Japan had\par ended its campaign to weaken its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushed the yen\par to a five-week high of 105.26 per dollar.\par     However, it quickly fell back to around 105.77 on what\par market sources said was dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japan and\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would continue its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        was little moved but holding on\par the strong side of 1.69 per dollar in late morning trade.\par Dealers said it showed a strengthening bias, with resistance at\par 1.6870.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think with dollar/yen trending lower, I would say we\par would see the dollar sold (against Sing) on rallies," said one\par trader, adding the region had lagged yen gains last week\par because there was some buying of the yen against regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Last week there were some yen crosses going through, so\par the dollar/Sing and the dollar/region was rather supported even\par though dollar/yen was coming off,  but I think that should be\par over this week."\par     The Thai baht        was sitting at 39.50 per dollar,\par showing little reaction to a weekend bomb attack that wounded\par 30 people in the country's Muslim south.\par     The Philippine peso        remained stuck near record lows,\par trading around 56.40 per dollar, while the Indonesian rupiah\par   edged up towards 8,600 per dollar.\par     In Taiwan, President Chen Shui-bian's decision to agree to\par a full judicial recount of votes in the disputed March 20\par election eased political tensions and lifted local markets.\par     The main stock index         was up around five percent in\par early trade, and the Taiwan dollar  lead Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains on the day.\par     The Korean won                  was also stronger, rising\par on the yen gains and expectations that local exporters would\par increase dollar sales towards month-end.\par     The end of the Japanese fiscal year on Wednesday is\par expected to limit volumes in the early part of the week, as\par institutions were expected to have already closed their books.\par     Markets are also waiting for indicators such as Japan's\par tankan survey of corporate sentiment on Thursday and the U.S.\par employment report on Friday for direction, amid some questions\par about the strength of the global economy as the European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has hinted it may need to cut interest rates.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0301 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.52         105.61       +0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.6895         1.6895        0.00\par  Taiwan dlr      33.150         33.274       +0.37\par  Korean won     1155.00        1157.70       +0.23\par  Baht             39.51          39.54       +0.08\par  Peso             56.38          56.43       +0.08\par  Rupiah         8610.00        8620.00       +0.12\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.52         107.31       +1.70\par  Sing dlr        1.6895         1.6978       +0.49\par  Taiwan dlr      33.150         33.978       +2.50\par  Korean won     1155.00        1192.00       +3.20\par  Baht             39.51          39.59       +0.19\par  Peso             56.38          55.49       -1.58\par  Rupiah         8610.00        8410.00       -2.32.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040329e03t000ei\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\a